    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once for performance\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N1 = int(input_data[0])\n    N2 = int(input_data[1])\n    M = int(input_data[2])\n    \n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N1 + N2 + 1)]\n    ptr = 3\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(input_data[ptr])\n        v = int(input_data[ptr+1])\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n        ptr += 2\n        \n    def bfs(start_node, limit_min, limit_max):\n        \"\"\"\n        Standard BFS to find the shortest path from start_node \n        to all other nodes within the range [limit_min, limit_max].\n        \"\"\"\n        dist = [-1] * (N1 + N2 + 1)\n        dist[start_node] = 0\n        queue = deque([start_node])\n        \n        while queue:\n            u = queue.popleft()\n            for v in adj[u]:\n                if limit_min <= v <= limit_max and dist[v] == -1:\n                    dist[v] = dist[u] + 1\n                    queue.append(v)\n        return dist\n\n    # The path from 1 to (N1+N2) will consist of:\n    # (path from 1 to u in the first component) + (edge u-v) + (path from v to N1+N2 in the second component)\n    # Length = dist(1, u) + 1 + dist(v, N1+N2)\n    # To maximize this, we maximize dist(1, u) and dist(v, N1+N2) independently.\n    \n    # BFS from node 1 restricted to the first component [1, N1]\n    dist1 = bfs(1, 1, N1)\n    # BFS from node (N1+N2) restricted to the second component [N1+1, N1+N2]\n    dist2 = bfs(N1 + N2, N1 + 1, N1 + N2)\n    \n    # Find the maximum distance from 1 to any u in [1, N1]\n    max_d1 = 0\n    for i in range(1, N1 + 1):\n        if dist1[i] > max_d1:\n            max_d1 = dist1[i]\n            \n    # Find the maximum distance from (N1+N2) to any v in [N1+1, N1+N2]\n    max_d2 = 0\n    for i in range(N1 + 1, N1 + N2 + 1):\n        if dist2[i] > max_d2:\n            max_d2 = dist2[i]\n            \n    # The result is max_dist(1, u) + 1 (for the new edge) + max_dist(v, N1+N2)\n    print(max_d1 + max_d2 + 1)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
