      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    In a regular pentagon with vertices A, B, C, D, E (arranged in order),\n    the distance between two vertices depends only on how many steps \n    separate them along the perimeter.\n    \n    Distance can be:\n    1 step: (A,B), (B,C), (C,D), (D,E), (E,A) - Side length\n    2 steps: (A,C), (B,D), (C,E), (D,A), (E,B) - Diagonal length\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    s = input_data[0]\n    t = input_data[1]\n    \n    # Define vertices in order\n    vertices = \"ABCDE\"\n    \n    def get_dist_type(pair):\n        # Get indices of the two vertices\n        idx1 = vertices.find(pair[0])\n        idx2 = vertices.find(pair[1])\n        \n        # Calculate the absolute difference in indices\n        diff = abs(idx1 - idx2)\n        \n        # In a circle of 5, the distance is the minimum of the clockwise \n        # and counter-clockwise steps.\n        # Distance is min(diff, 5 - diff)\n        return min(diff, 5 - diff)\n\n    # Compare the distance types for the two pairs\n    if get_dist_type(s) == get_dist_type(t):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
