    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxEnergy(energy, k):\n    n = len(energy)\n    # We use a dynamic programming approach.\n    # dp[i] will store the maximum energy gained if we start the jumping process at index i.\n    # We iterate backwards because the value at index i depends on the value at index i + k.\n    dp = [0] * n\n    \n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        if i + k < n:\n            # If we can jump further, the energy gained is current energy + energy from the jump destination\n            dp[i] = energy[i] + dp[i + k]\n        else:\n            # If we cannot jump further, the energy gained is just the current energy\n            dp[i] = energy[i]\n            \n    return max(dp)\n```",
