    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef countServers(n, logs, x, queries):\n    # Sort logs by time to use a sliding window approach\n    logs.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n    \n    # We need to handle queries in increasing order of time to maintain the window\n    # Store original indices to return the result in the correct order\n    sorted_queries = sorted([(q, i) for i, q in enumerate(queries)])\n    \n    ans = [0] * len(queries)\n    server_counts = [0] * (n + 1)\n    active_servers = 0\n    \n    left = 0 # Left pointer for logs window\n    right = 0 # Right pointer for logs window\n    \n    for q_val, q_idx in sorted_queries:\n        # The window for the current query is [q_val - x, q_val]\n        window_start = q_val - x\n        window_end = q_val\n        \n        # Expand the right boundary to include logs up to window_end\n        while right < len(logs) and logs[right][1] <= window_end:\n            s_id = logs[right][0]\n            if server_counts[s_id] == 0:\n                active_servers += 1\n            server_counts[s_id] += 1\n            right += 1\n            \n        # Shrink the left boundary to remove logs before window_start\n        while left < len(logs) and logs[left][1] < window_start:\n            s_id = logs[left][0]\n            server_counts[s_id] -= 1\n            if server_counts[s_id] == 0:\n                active_servers -= 1\n            left += 1\n            \n        # The number of servers that did NOT receive requests is total - active\n        ans[q_idx] = n - active_servers\n        \n    return ans\n```",
