    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfRightTriangles(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    row_counts = [0] * rows\n    col_counts = [0] * cols\n    \n    # Precompute the number of 1s in each row and each column\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                row_counts[r] += 1\n                col_counts[c] += 1\n                \n    total_triangles = 0\n    \n    # A right triangle is formed by a vertex (r, c) that is 1, \n    # combined with any other 1 in the same row and any other 1 in the same column.\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                # Number of other 1s in the same row is (row_counts[r] - 1)\n                # Number of other 1s in the same column is (col_counts[c] - 1)\n                total_triangles += (row_counts[r] - 1) * (col_counts[c] - 1)\n                \n    return total_triangles\n```",
