    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Reads the scores of Team Takahashi (top 1-9) and Team Aoki (bottom 1-8)\n    from stdin and calculates the minimum runs Team Aoki needs in the bottom \n    of the ninth to win (score strictly more than Takahashi).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read all input from stdin and split into a list of integers\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    # First 9 values are Team Takahashi's runs (A_1 to A_9)\n    # Remaining 8 values are Team Aoki's runs (B_1 to B_8)\n    a_scores = list(map(int, input_data[:9]))\n    b_scores = list(map(int, input_data[9:]))\n\n    total_takahashi = sum(a_scores)\n    total_aoki_current = sum(b_scores)\n\n    # For Team Aoki to win, their total must be > total_takahashi.\n    # Let X be the runs scored in the bottom of the 9th.\n    # total_aoki_current + X >= total_takahashi + 1\n    # X >= total_takahashi - total_aoki_current + 1\n    \n    needed = total_takahashi - total_aoki_current + 1\n    \n    # Since the problem constraints state Takahashi's score is not less than Aoki's,\n    # needed will always be at least 1.\n    print(needed)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
