    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestValidSubstring(word: str, forbidden: list[str]) -> int:\n    forbidden_set = set(forbidden)\n    max_len = 0\n    n = len(word)\n    left = 0\n    \n    for right in range(n):\n        # Check all substrings ending at 'right' that could be in forbidden.\n        # Since forbidden[i].length <= 10, we only need to check back 10 characters.\n        for length in range(1, 11):\n            start = right - length + 1\n            if start < left:\n                break\n            \n            if word[start:right + 1] in forbidden_set:\n                # If a forbidden substring is found, the new 'left' boundary \n                # must move past the start of this forbidden substring.\n                left = start + 1\n                # Since we are moving 'left' forward, we can stop checking \n                # shorter forbidden strings for this specific 'right' index\n                # because we already jumped past them.\n                break\n        \n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n        \n    return max_len\n```",
