    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(s):\n    n = len(s)\n    # dp[i] will store the minimum number of balanced substrings to partition s[:i]\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # To track character counts for the current substring ending at i\n        counts = {}\n        distinct_chars = 0\n        \n        # Check all possible starting points j for the last substring s[j:i]\n        for j in range(i - 1, -1, -1):\n            char = s[j]\n            if char not in counts:\n                counts[char] = 0\n                distinct_chars += 1\n            counts[char] += 1\n            \n            # A substring is balanced if:\n            # (Total length) is divisible by (Number of distinct characters)\n            # AND each distinct character appears (Total length / Number of distinct characters) times.\n            substring_len = i - j\n            if substring_len % distinct_chars == 0:\n                freq = substring_len // distinct_chars\n                is_balanced = True\n                for char_count in counts.values():\n                    if char_count != freq:\n                        is_balanced = False\n                        break\n                \n                if is_balanced:\n                    dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n                    \n    return dp[n]\n```",
