    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin and strip whitespace\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    \n    if not s:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        return\n\n    # An Extended ABC string must match the regular expression A*B*C*\n    # We can verify this by checking if the string is sorted.\n    # Since 'A' < 'B' < 'C' in lexicographical order, \n    # a string consisting of A, B, and C is an Extended ABC string \n    # if and only if it is sorted.\n    \n    if list(s) == sorted(s):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
