      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef max_distance(moves: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum distance from the origin after n moves.\n    Each '_' can be treated as either 'L' or 'R'.\n    To maximize distance, we should consistently move in one direction \n    whenever we have a choice ('_').\n    \"\"\"\n    # Case 1: Try to go as far left as possible\n    # Treat '_' as 'L'\n    left_dist = 0\n    for char in moves:\n        if char == 'L' or char == '_':\n            left_dist -= 1\n        else:\n            left_dist += 1\n            \n    # Case 2: Try to go as far right as possible\n    # Treat '_' as 'R'\n    right_dist = 0\n    for char in moves:\n        if char == 'R' or char == '_':\n            right_dist += 1\n        else:\n            right_dist -= 1\n            \n    # The result is the maximum absolute distance achieved from either strategy\n    return max(abs(left_dist), abs(right_dist))\n```",
