      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input using fast I/O\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    ptr = 0\n    N = int(input_data[ptr])\n    M = int(input_data[ptr+1])\n    K = int(input_data[ptr+2])\n    ptr += 3\n    \n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(input_data[ptr])\n        v = int(input_data[ptr+1])\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n        ptr += 2\n    \n    # We want to find vertices reachable from guards within their stamina h_i.\n    # This can be solved using a Dijkstra-like approach where we track the \n    # maximum remaining stamina reaching a vertex.\n    # dist[v] will store the maximum stamina of a guard that can reach vertex v.\n    # If dist[v] >= 0, it means the vertex is guarded.\n    \n    # Initial stamina at each vertex is -1 (not reached)\n    stamina = [-1] * (N + 1)\n    pq = deque()\n    \n    # Guards as starting points\n    # Since stamina decreases by 1 per edge, we can use a priority queue\n    # or, since edge weights are 1, a modified BFS if we handle levels.\n    # However, because different guards start with different h_i, \n    # we use a Dijkstra approach with a max-heap or simply use a \n    # priority queue to always expand the node with the most remaining stamina.\n    \n    import heapq\n    max_heap = []\n    \n    for _ in range(K):\n        p = int(input_data[ptr])\n        h = int(input_data[ptr+1])\n        ptr += 2\n        if h > stamina[p]:\n            stamina[p] = h\n            heapq.heappush(max_heap, (-h, p))\n            \n    while max_heap:\n        curr_h_neg, u = heapq.heappop(max_heap)\n        curr_h = -curr_h_neg\n        \n        if curr_h < stamina[u]:\n            continue\n        \n        if curr_h > 0:\n            for v in adj[u]:\n                if stamina[v] < curr_h - 1:\n                    stamina[v] = curr_h - 1\n                    heapq.heappush(max_heap, (-(curr_h - 1), v))\n                    \n    # Collect all vertices where stamina is >= 0\n    guarded = [i for i in range(1, N + 1) if stamina[i] >= 0]\n    \n    # Output the number of guarded vertices and their IDs\n    print(len(guarded))\n    print(*(guarded))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
