    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Reading input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    ptr = 0\n    N = int(input_data[ptr])\n    ptr += 1\n    \n    A_initial = input_data[ptr : ptr + N]\n    ptr += N\n    \n    Q = int(input_data[ptr])\n    ptr += 1\n    \n    # Since we need fast insertions and deletions in a sequence \n    # where positions are relative to existing values, a Doubly Linked List \n    # implemented using a dictionary is the most efficient approach.\n    # next_val[x] stores the element immediately after x.\n    # prev_val[x] stores the element immediately before x.\n    next_val = {}\n    prev_val = {}\n    \n    # Initialize the sequence\n    for i in range(N):\n        curr = A_initial[i]\n        if i < N - 1:\n            next_val[curr] = A_initial[i+1]\n        else:\n            next_val[curr] = None\n        \n        if i > 0:\n            prev_val[curr] = A_initial[i-1]\n        else:\n            prev_val[curr] = None\n            \n    head = A_initial[0]\n    \n    for _ in range(Q):\n        q_type = input_data[ptr]\n        ptr += 1\n        \n        if q_type == '1':\n            x = input_data[ptr]\n            y = input_data[ptr + 1]\n            ptr += 2\n            \n            # Insert y after x\n            after_x = next_val.get(x)\n            next_val[x] = y\n            prev_val[y] = x\n            next_val[y] = after_x\n            if after_x is not None:\n                prev_val[after_x] = y\n                \n        elif q_type == '2':\n            x = input_data[ptr]\n            ptr += 1\n            \n            # Remove x\n            before_x = prev_val.get(x)\n            after_x = next_val.get(x)\n            \n            if before_x is not None:\n                next_val[before_x] = after_x\n            else:\n                # x was the head\n                head = after_x\n                \n            if after_x is not None:\n                prev_val[after_x] = before_x\n            \n            # Clean up to avoid memory leak / logic errors\n            if x in next_val: del next_val[x]\n            if x in prev_val: del prev_val[x]\n\n    # Reconstruct the final sequence starting from head\n    result = []\n    curr = head\n    while curr is not None:\n        result.append(curr)\n        curr = next_val.get(curr)\n    \n    print(\" \".join(result))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
