      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read the input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    # A is not the culprit, B is not the culprit\n    A = int(input_data[0])\n    B = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    # The set of all possible suspects\n    suspects = {1, 2, 3}\n    \n    # Remove the people who are known NOT to be the culprit\n    suspects.discard(A)\n    suspects.discard(B)\n    \n    # If only one person remains, that person is uniquely identified as the culprit\n    if len(suspects) == 1:\n        print(list(suspects)[0])\n    else:\n        # Otherwise, the culprit cannot be uniquely identified\n        print(\"-1\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
