      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once for efficiency\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    W = int(input_data[1])\n    N = int(input_data[2])\n    \n    # Using a 2D array to store whether a square is holed.\n    # dp[i][j] will store the side length of the largest holeless square \n    # whose bottom-right corner is (i, j).\n    # To save memory and handle constraints (3000x3000), \n    # we only need the previous row of DP values.\n    \n    # grid[i][j] = 1 if holed, 0 otherwise.\n    # However, creating a full 3000x3000 grid might be memory intensive.\n    # We can process row by row.\n    \n    holed_set = set()\n    idx = 3\n    for _ in range(N):\n        r = int(input_data[idx])\n        c = int(input_data[idx+1])\n        holed_set.add((r, c))\n        idx += 2\n        \n    # dp[j] will store the max side length of holeless square ending at (current_row, j)\n    dp = [0] * (W + 1)\n    total_holeless = 0\n    \n    for i in range(1, H + 1):\n        prev_dp_diag = 0 # represents dp[i-1][j-1]\n        for j in range(1, W + 1):\n            temp = dp[j] # store dp[i-1][j] for the next j's diag\n            if (i, j) in holed_set:\n                dp[j] = 0\n            else:\n                # Standard DP for largest square in binary matrix:\n                # dp[i][j] = min(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1], dp[i-1][j-1]) + 1\n                # dp[j] is dp[i-1][j], dp[j-1] is dp[i][j-1], prev_dp_diag is dp[i-1][j-1]\n                res = min(dp[j], dp[j-1], prev_dp_diag) + 1\n                dp[j] = res\n                total_holeless += res\n            prev_dp_diag = temp\n            \n    print(total_holeless)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
