      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read N from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    # A is 1-indexed in the problem, we convert it to 0-indexed internally\n    # a[i] is the destination of the edge starting at vertex i\n    a = [int(x) - 1 for x in input_data[1:]]\n    \n    # To find a cycle in a functional graph (where every node has out-degree 1),\n    # we can start at any node and follow the edges until we hit a node \n    # that has already been visited.\n    \n    visited = [False] * n\n    # Path stores the order of nodes visited in the current traversal\n    path = []\n    # Position stores the index of the node in the path list for O(1) lookup\n    pos = [-1] * n\n    \n    # Start traversal from node 0 (since a solution is guaranteed to exist)\n    curr = 0\n    while not visited[curr]:\n        visited[curr] = True\n        pos[curr] = len(path)\n        path.append(curr)\n        curr = a[curr]\n    \n    # curr is now the start of the cycle\n    cycle_start_idx = pos[curr]\n    cycle = path[cycle_start_idx:]\n    \n    # The output requires 1-based indexing\n    print(len(cycle))\n    print(*(v + 1 for v in cycle))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
