      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(purchaseAmount):\n    # To round to the nearest multiple of 10, we look at the last digit.\n    # If the last digit is 5 or greater, we round up.\n    # If it is less than 5, we round down.\n    # This logic ensures the distance is minimized and the larger multiple is picked in case of a tie.\n    \n    remainder = purchaseAmount % 10\n    if remainder >= 5:\n        roundedAmount = purchaseAmount + (10 - remainder)\n    else:\n        roundedAmount = purchaseAmount - remainder\n        \n    return 100 - roundedAmount\n```",
