    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxGold(n, offers):\n    # Use a list of lists to store offers ending at each house index\n    # adj[i] will store pairs of (start_index, gold) for offers that end at house i\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for start, end, gold in offers:\n        adj[end].append((start, gold))\n    \n    # dp[i] stores the maximum gold that can be earned from houses 0 to i-1\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        # Option 1: House i is not sold to any buyer ending at i\n        # The max gold is the same as the max gold earned up to house i-1\n        dp[i + 1] = dp[i]\n        \n        # Option 2: House i is sold to a buyer who wants range [start, i]\n        # We iterate through all offers that end at index i\n        for start, gold in adj[i]:\n            # The earnings would be the gold from this offer plus \n            # the max gold earned from houses before the start of this range\n            dp[i + 1] = max(dp[i + 1], dp[start] + gold)\n            \n    return dp[n]\n```",
