      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumChanges(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    To make a binary string beautiful, it must be partitionable into \n    substrings of even length where each substring consists of only 0s or 1s.\n    This effectively means that for every pair of characters at indices (0,1), (2,3), etc.,\n    the two characters in the pair must be identical.\n    \"\"\"\n    changes = 0\n    # Iterate through the string in steps of 2\n    for i in range(0, len(s), 2):\n        # If the two characters in the current pair are different, \n        # we need one change to make them the same (either both '0' or both '1').\n        if s[i] != s[i+1]:\n            changes += 1\n    return changes\n```",
