      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    ptr = 0\n    t = int(input_data[ptr])\n    ptr += 1\n    \n    results = []\n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input_data[ptr])\n        ptr += 1\n        a = []\n        for _ in range(n):\n            a.append(int(input_data[ptr]))\n            ptr += 1\n        \n        # To maximize the product by adding 1 to one element,\n        # we should add it to the smallest element.\n        # Example: (2, 3) -> 2*3=6. Options: (3, 3)=9 or (2, 4)=8. \n        # Adding to the minimum maximizes the relative increase.\n        \n        # Find the index of the minimum element\n        min_val = min(a)\n        min_idx = a.index(min_val)\n        \n        # Create a copy and increment the minimum element\n        modified_a = list(a)\n        modified_a[min_idx] += 1\n        \n        # Calculate product\n        product = 1\n        for x in modified_a:\n            product *= x\n        \n        results.append(str(product))\n    \n    # Print all results separated by newline\n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results) + '\\n')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
