    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\n# Increase recursion depth for deep trees\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10**6)\n\ndef solve():\n    # Use fast I/O\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    if N == 1:\n        print(1)\n        return\n\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(N - 1):\n        u = int(input_data[idx])\n        v = int(input_data[idx + 1])\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n        idx += 2\n\n    # The problem asks for the minimum number of operations to delete vertex 1.\n    # Vertex 1 can be deleted if it becomes a leaf (degree <= 1).\n    # Let's root the tree at vertex 1. \n    # To make vertex 1 a leaf, we must completely delete all but one of its subtrees.\n    # If vertex 1 is already a leaf (degree 1), the answer is 1.\n    # Otherwise, we need to find the subtree rooted at one of vertex 1's children \n    # that contains the most nodes, and delete all other subtrees.\n    # The cost to delete vertex 1 would be (N - size of the largest subtree attached to 1) + 1.\n    # Wait, the logic is: vertex 1 can be deleted as soon as its degree is 1.\n    # To reduce degree(1) to 1, we must remove all nodes in all subtrees except for the largest one.\n    # Total nodes = N. \n    # Nodes in the largest subtree = max_subtree_size.\n    # Nodes to remove to make vertex 1 have degree 1 = (N - 1) - max_subtree_size.\n    # Then we perform one final operation to delete vertex 1 itself.\n    # Total = N - max_subtree_size.\n    \n    if len(adj[1]) <= 1:\n        print(1)\n        return\n\n    # BFS to calculate subtree sizes rooted at 1\n    subtree_size = [0] * (N + 1)\n    parent = [0] * (N + 1)\n    order = []\n    stack = [1]\n    visited = [False] * (N + 1)\n    visited[1] = True\n    \n    # Iterative BFS/DFS to avoid recursion limits and get processing order\n    queue = [1]\n    visited = [False] * (N + 1)\n    visited[1] = True\n    head = 0\n    while head < len(queue):\n        u = queue[head]\n        head += 1\n        order.append(u)\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if not visited[v]:\n                visited[v] = True\n                parent[v] = u\n                queue.append(v)\n                \n    # Process in reverse topological order to compute subtree sizes\n    for u in reversed(order):\n        subtree_size[u] = 1\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != parent[u]:\n                subtree_size[u] += subtree_size[v]\n                \n    # Find the largest subtree among the children of vertex 1\n    max_size = 0\n    for v in adj[1]:\n        # Since 1 is root, any neighbor is a child\n        if subtree_size[v] > max_size:\n            max_size = subtree_size[v]\n            \n    print(N - max_size)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
