    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumLength(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest semi-repetitive substring.\n    A semi-repetitive string contains at most one pair of identical consecutive digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    max_len = 0\n    left = 0\n    repeat_idx = -1  # Index of the first character of the last encountered duplicate pair\n\n    for right in range(n):\n        # Check if we found a consecutive pair\n        if right > 0 and s[right] == s[right - 1]:\n            # If a repeat already existed, we must move 'left' to exclude the previous repeat\n            if repeat_idx != -1:\n                left = repeat_idx + 1\n            # Update the index of the current repeat\n            repeat_idx = right - 1\n            \n        # Calculate current window length and update max_len\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n        \n    return max_len\n```",
