      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import permutations\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read H and W\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    W = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    idx = 2\n    A = []\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = []\n        for j in range(W):\n            row.append(int(input_data[idx]))\n            idx += 1\n        A.append(row)\n        \n    B = []\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = []\n        for j in range(W):\n            row.append(int(input_data[idx]))\n            idx += 1\n        B.append(row)\n\n    # Function to calculate minimum swaps to transform one permutation to another\n    # This is equal to the number of inversions in the permutation that maps \n    # the initial order to the target order.\n    def get_swaps(p):\n        n = len(p)\n        swaps = 0\n        # Create a copy to avoid mutating\n        arr = list(p)\n        for i in range(n):\n            # Find where the element that should be at position i is currently\n            # Since we need the minimum adjacent swaps, we simulate insertion sort or inversion count\n            # But the permutation p here is already defined as: target[i] = source[p[i]]\n            pass\n        # Standard inversion count for the permutation p\n        inv = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                if p[i] > p[j]:\n                    inv += 1\n        return inv\n\n    min_total_ops = float('inf')\n    found = False\n\n    # Iterate through all possible permutations of rows and columns\n    # H and W are small (<= 5), so 5! * 5! = 120 * 120 = 14,400 iterations.\n    for row_p in permutations(range(H)):\n        for col_p in permutations(range(W)):\n            # Check if applying these permutations to A yields B\n            # B[i][j] should be A[row_p[i]][col_p[j]]\n            match = True\n            for i in range(H):\n                for j in range(W):\n                    if A[row_p[i]][col_p[j]] != B[i][j]:\n                        match = False\n                        break\n                if not match:\n                    break\n            \n            if match:\n                found = True\n                # Minimum adjacent swaps to transform (0,1,..,N-1) to row_p is inversion count of row_p\n                ops = get_swaps(row_p) + get_swaps(col_p)\n                if ops < min_total_ops:\n                    min_total_ops = ops\n\n    if not found:\n        print(\"-1\")\n    else:\n        print(min_total_ops)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
