    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    The plant's height on the morning of day 'd' is the sum of growth \n    from night 0 to night d-1.\n    Growth on night i is 2^i.\n    Total height on morning of day d = 2^0 + 2^1 + ... + 2^(d-1) = 2^d - 1.\n    We need the smallest d such that 2^d - 1 > H, which is 2^d > H + 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # Start from day 0 and increment until the condition is met\n    d = 0\n    while True:\n        # height_morning_d = (2 ** d) - 1\n        if (1 << d) - 1 > H:\n            print(d)\n            break\n        d += 1\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
