      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(input_data)\n    \n    # The rules follow a pattern:\n    # 10^0 to 10^3-1: No truncation (divisor 1)\n    # 10^3 to 10^4-1: Truncate 1 digit (divisor 10)\n    # 10^4 to 10^5-1: Truncate 2 digits (divisor 100)\n    # ... and so on.\n    # The number of digits to truncate is effectively (length of N) - 3, \n    # provided N >= 1000.\n    \n    if n <= 10**3 - 1:\n        print(n)\n    elif n <= 10**4 - 1:\n        # Truncate ones digit: floor(n/10) * 10\n        print((n // 10) * 10)\n    elif n <= 10**5 - 1:\n        # Truncate tens and below: floor(n/100) * 100\n        print((n // 100) * 100)\n    elif n <= 10**6 - 1:\n        # Truncate hundreds and below: floor(n/1000) * 1000\n        print((n // 1000) * 1000)\n    elif n <= 10**7 - 1:\n        # Truncate thousands and below\n        print((n // 10000) * 10000)\n    elif n <= 10**8 - 1:\n        # Truncate ten-thousands and below\n        print((n // 100000) * 100000)\n    elif n <= 10**9 - 1:\n        # Truncate hundred-thousands and below\n        print((n // 1000000) * 1000000)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
