      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef buyChocolates(prices, money):\n    # To minimize the sum of two chocolates, we find the two cheapest ones.\n    # Sorting the prices array allows us to easily access the two smallest values.\n    prices.sort()\n    \n    # The two smallest prices are at indices 0 and 1.\n    min_cost = prices[0] + prices[1]\n    \n    # Check if we can afford both chocolates without going into debt.\n    if min_cost <= money:\n        return money - min_cost\n    else:\n        # If we cannot afford the two cheapest, we cannot buy any two chocolates.\n        return money\n```",
