      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Reads N, M, and P from stdin and calculates the number of full moon days \n    between day 1 and day N.\n    \n    The full moons occur on days: M, M+P, M+2P, ...\n    We need to find the number of integers k >= 0 such that M + k*P <= N.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    m = int(input_data[1])\n    p = int(input_data[2])\n    \n    # If the first full moon is after day N, there are 0 days.\n    if m > n:\n        print(0)\n    else:\n        # We need to solve for k: M + k*P <= N\n        # k*P <= N - M\n        # k <= (N - M) / P\n        # Since k starts from 0, the total count is floor((N - M) / P) + 1\n        count = ((n - m) // p) + 1\n        print(count)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
