    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    ptr = 0\n    N = int(input_data[ptr])\n    M = int(input_data[ptr + 1])\n    ptr += 2\n    \n    products = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        p = int(input_data[ptr])\n        c = int(input_data[ptr + 1])\n        # Store functions as a set for efficient subset checking\n        f = set(map(int, input_data[ptr + 2 : ptr + 2 + c]))\n        products.append({'p': p, 'f': f})\n        ptr += 2 + c\n    \n    # We are looking for i and j such that product i is \"strictly inferior\" \n    # or product j is \"strictly superior\" based on the problem text.\n    # Conditions for product i to be \"worse\" than product j:\n    # 1. P_i >= P_j\n    # 2. Functions of i are a subset of functions of j\n    # 3. Either P_i > P_j OR (Functions of i are a proper subset of functions of j)\n    \n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(N):\n            if i == j:\n                continue\n            \n            pi, fi = products[i]['p'], products[i]['f']\n            pj, fj = products[j]['p'], products[j]['f']\n            \n            # Condition 1: P_i >= P_j\n            if pi >= pj:\n                # Condition 2: The j-th product has all functions of the i-th product\n                if fi.issubset(fj):\n                    # Condition 3: P_i > P_j or j has more functions than i\n                    if pi > pj or len(fj) > len(fi):\n                        print(\"Yes\")\n                        return\n\n    print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
