    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_substrings(s: str, c: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total number of substrings of s that start and end with character c.\n    The number of such substrings is equal to the number of ways to choose 2 indices \n    where s[i] == c, plus the number of indices where s[i] == c (single character substrings).\n    This is equivalent to n * (n + 1) // 2, where n is the count of character c in s.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = s.count(c)\n    return n * (n + 1) // 2\n```",
