    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once for efficiency\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # Dictionary to store the minimum deliciousness encountered for each color\n    # Key: Color (C_i), Value: Minimum deliciousness (A_i) for that color\n    min_deliciousness_per_color = {}\n    \n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(N):\n        a = int(input_data[idx])\n        c = int(input_data[idx+1])\n        idx += 2\n        \n        if c in min_deliciousness_per_color:\n            if a < min_deliciousness_per_color[c]:\n                min_deliciousness_per_color[c] = a\n        else:\n            min_deliciousness_per_color[c] = a\n            \n    # We want to maximize the minimum deliciousness across all chosen colors\n    # The values in the dictionary are the \"minimum possible deliciousness\" for each color\n    result = max(min_deliciousness_per_color.values())\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
