      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Reads an integer X from stdin and prints ceil(X/10).\n    In Python, the integer division operator // performs floor division.\n    The ceiling of (a / b) can be calculated using the formula:\n    ceil(a / b) = -(-a // b)\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read the input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    try:\n        x = int(input_data)\n    except ValueError:\n        return\n\n    # To compute ceil(x / 10) using integer arithmetic:\n    # Python's // is floor. -(-x // 10) is equivalent to ceil(x / 10).\n    # Example x = 27: -(-27 // 10) = -(-3) = 3\n    # Example x = -13: -(-(-13) // 10) = -(13 // 10) = -(1) = -1\n    # Example x = 40: -(-40 // 10) = -(-4) = 4\n    # Example x = -20: -(-(-20) // 10) = -(20 // 10) = -(2) = -2\n    \n    result = -(-x // 10)\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
