    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    A = list(map(int, input_data[1:]))\n    \n    # Handle zeros separately:\n    # If A_i = 0, then A_i * A_j = 0, which is 0^2 (a square number).\n    # Any pair containing at least one zero satisfies the condition.\n    zeros_count = 0\n    non_zeros = []\n    for x in A:\n        if x == 0:\n            zeros_count += 1\n        else:\n            non_zeros.append(x)\n            \n    # Total pairs involving at least one zero:\n    # Pairs of (0, 0) + Pairs of (0, non-zero)\n    # = zeros_count * (zeros_count - 1) // 2 + zeros_count * (N - zeros_count)\n    ans = (zeros_count * (zeros_count - 1)) // 2 + zeros_count * (N - zeros_count)\n    \n    # For non-zero integers, A_i * A_j is a square if and only if \n    # their square-free parts are the same.\n    # Square-free part of x is x divided by the largest square that divides x.\n    \n    # Precompute smallest prime factor or just compute square-free part iteratively\n    # since max A_i is 2*10^5.\n    max_val = 200000\n    square_free_parts = {}\n    \n    # To optimize, we can precompute square-free parts for all numbers up to max_val\n    # using a sieve-like approach.\n    sf = list(range(max_val + 1))\n    for i in range(2, int(max_val**0.5) + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        # If i^2 divides sf[j], keep dividing until it doesn't.\n        # However, a simpler way is to mark all multiples of i^2.\n        for j in range(square, max_val + 1, square):\n            while sf[j] % square == 0:\n                sf[j] //= square\n                \n    counts = {}\n    for x in non_zeros:\n        part = sf[x]\n        counts[part] = counts.get(part, 0) + 1\n        \n    for part in counts:\n        c = counts[part]\n        ans += (c * (c - 1)) // 2\n        \n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
