      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    The game logic:\n    Vanya wins if he can make the number divisible by 3 in his first move.\n    If n is already divisible by 3, adding 1 or subtracting 1 will make it \n    not divisible by 3 (n+1 or n-1). Vova will then try to move it back \n    to a state where Vanya cannot win.\n    \n    Specifically, if n % 3 == 0, Vanya's move makes it n % 3 == 1 or 2. \n    Then Vova can simply reverse Vanya's move to bring it back to n % 3 == 0.\n    Since Vova can always return the number to a multiple of 3, Vanya can \n    never win on his turn if the starting n is already divisible by 3.\n    \n    If n % 3 != 0, Vanya can immediately make the number divisible by 3 \n    (by adding 1 if n%3 == 2 or subtracting 1 if n%3 == 1) and win on the first move.\n    \"\"\"\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    t = int(input_data[0])\n    results = []\n    \n    for i in range(1, t + 1):\n        n = int(input_data[i])\n        if n % 3 == 0:\n            results.append(\"Second\")\n        else:\n            results.append(\"First\")\n            \n    print(\"\\n\".join(results))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
