    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findPeaks(mountain):\n    peaks = []\n    # A peak cannot be the first or last element, so we iterate from index 1 to len(mountain) - 2\n    for i in range(1, len(mountain) - 1):\n        # Check if the current element is strictly greater than its neighbors\n        if mountain[i] > mountain[i - 1] and mountain[i] > mountain[i + 1]:\n            peaks.append(i)\n    return peaks\n```",
