      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxFrequency(nums, k):\n    nums.sort()\n    left = 0\n    total_sum = 0\n    max_freq = 0\n    \n    # Use a sliding window approach.\n    # For a window from index 'left' to 'right', to make all elements equal to nums[right],\n    # the cost is (nums[right] * window_length) - sum(elements in window).\n    for right in range(len(nums)):\n        total_sum += nums[right]\n        \n        # While the cost to make all elements in the current window equal to nums[right]\n        # exceeds k, shrink the window from the left.\n        while (nums[right] * (right - left + 1)) - total_sum > k:\n            total_sum -= nums[left]\n            left += 1\n            \n        # Update the maximum frequency found so far.\n        max_freq = max(max_freq, right - left + 1)\n        \n    return max_freq\n```",
