      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Increase recursion depth for deep dependency chains\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(300000)\n    \n    # Read all input at once and split by whitespace\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    \n    ptr = 1\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        C_i = int(input_data[ptr])\n        ptr += 1\n        for _ in range(C_i):\n            adj[i].append(int(input_data[ptr]))\n            ptr += 1\n            \n    # 1. Identify the set of books required to read book 1 using DFS\n    required = [False] * (N + 1)\n    stack = [1]\n    required[1] = True\n    \n    # Iterative DFS to find all reachable nodes from book 1\n    visited_search = [False] * (N + 1)\n    visited_search[1] = True\n    search_stack = [1]\n    while search_stack:\n        u = search_stack.pop()\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if not visited_search[v]:\n                visited_search[v] = True\n                required[v] = True\n                search_stack.append(v)\n    \n    # 2. Perform a topological sort on the subset of required books\n    # We only care about books that are required to read book 1\n    visited_topo = [False] * (N + 1)\n    result = []\n    \n    def dfs_topo(u):\n        visited_topo[u] = True\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            # Only traverse if the dependency is also part of the required set\n            if required[v] and not visited_topo[v]:\n                dfs_topo(v)\n        # Post-order traversal gives the order of reading\n        result.append(u)\n        \n    dfs_topo(1)\n    \n    # The result contains book 1 at the end, and it's in the order they should be read\n    # excluding book 1 as per the prompt.\n    # result list: [leaf_dependencies, ..., book 1]\n    # We need to print everything except the last element (which is book 1)\n    print(*(result[:-1]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
