\n00110\r\n10100",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    grid = []\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        grid.append(list(input_data[i]))\n\n    # Create a copy of the grid to store the result\n    res = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # The outer squares shift clockwise.\n    # This means:\n    # 1. Top row: B[0][j] = A[0][j-1] for j from 1 to N-1\n    # 2. Right col: B[i][N-1] = A[i-1][N-1] for i from 1 to N-1\n    # 3. Bottom row: B[N-1][j] = A[N-1][j+1] for j from N-2 down to 0\n    # 4. Left col: B[i][0] = A[i+1][0] for i from N-2 down to 0\n\n    # Top row shift\n    for j in range(1, N):\n        res[0][j] = grid[0][j-1]\n    \n    # Right column shift\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        res[i][N-1] = grid[i-1][N-1]\n        \n    # Bottom row shift\n    for j in range(N-2, -1, -1):\n        res[N-1][j] = grid[N-1][j+1]\n        \n    # Left column shift\n    for i in range(N-2, -1, -1):\n        res[i][0] = grid[i+1][0]\n\n    # Print the resulting grid\n    for row in res:\n        print(\"\".join(row))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
