      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    The goal is to repeatedly remove the leftmost occurrence of \"ABC\" \n    until no such substring exists. Using a stack-based approach \n    allows us to handle cases where removing \"ABC\" creates a new \"ABC\" \n    from the surrounding characters in O(N) time.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read input from stdin and strip whitespace\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    \n    stack = []\n    for char in s:\n        stack.append(char)\n        # Check if the last three characters added to the stack form \"ABC\"\n        if len(stack) >= 3:\n            if stack[-3] == 'A' and stack[-2] == 'B' and stack[-1] == 'C':\n                # Remove the \"ABC\" from the end of the stack\n                stack.pop()\n                stack.pop()\n                stack.pop()\n    \n    # Join the remaining characters in the stack to form the final string\n    print(\"\".join(stack))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
