    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Reads the current position N from stdin and finds the nearest water station.\n    Water stations are located every 5km (0, 5, 10, ..., 100).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read input from stdin\n    try:\n        line = sys.stdin.readline()\n        if not line:\n            return\n        n = int(line.strip())\n    except ValueError:\n        return\n\n    # The nearest multiple of 5 can be found by rounding N/5 to the nearest integer.\n    # In Python, round(2.5) is 2, but for this specific problem constraint,\n    # the prompt guarantees the nearest station is uniquely determined, \n    # meaning N will never be exactly halfway between two stations (e.g., 2.5, 7.5).\n    # Thus, a simple rounding approach or checking the two surrounding multiples works.\n    \n    lower_station = (n // 5) * 5\n    upper_station = lower_station + 5\n    \n    if (n - lower_station) < (upper_station - n):\n        print(lower_station)\n    else:\n        # Ensure we don't exceed the 100km limit, though constraints say N <= 100\n        print(min(upper_station, 100))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
