      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once and split by whitespace for efficiency\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    ptr = 0\n    t = int(input_data[ptr])\n    ptr += 1\n    \n    results = []\n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input_data[ptr])\n        k = int(input_data[ptr+1])\n        s = input_data[ptr+2]\n        ptr += 3\n        \n        operations = 0\n        i = 0\n        while i < n:\n            # Find the first occurrence of a black cell 'B'\n            if s[i] == 'B':\n                # Perform an operation starting at this index\n                # This covers cells from i to i + k - 1\n                operations += 1\n                i += k\n            else:\n                # Move to the next cell if the current one is white\n                i += 1\n        \n        results.append(str(operations))\n    \n    # Print all results separated by newlines\n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results) + '\\n')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
