      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    # Parse the input into a 9x9 grid\n    grid = []\n    for i in range(9):\n        row = [int(x) for x in input_data[i*9 : (i+1)*9]]\n        grid.append(row)\n        \n    target_set = set(range(1, 10))\n    \n    # 1. Check each row\n    for row in grid:\n        if set(row) != target_set:\n            print(\"No\")\n            return\n            \n    # 2. Check each column\n    for j in range(9):\n        column = [grid[i][j] for i in range(9)]\n        if set(column) != target_set:\n            print(\"No\")\n            return\n            \n    # 3. Check each 3x3 sub-grid\n    for row_offset in range(0, 9, 3):\n        for col_offset in range(0, 9, 3):\n            block = []\n            for i in range(3):\n                for j in range(3):\n                    block.append(grid[row_offset + i][col_offset + j])\n            if set(block) != target_set:\n                print(\"No\")\n                return\n                \n    # If all conditions are satisfied\n    print(\"Yes\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
