    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minCost(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    The cost of the array is the sum of the first elements of the 3 disjoint contiguous subarrays.\n    Since the subarrays are contiguous and cover the whole array:\n    1. The first subarray must start at index 0. Cost = nums[0].\n    2. The second subarray starts at index i (1 <= i <= n-2). Cost = nums[i].\n    3. The third subarray starts at index j (i+1 <= j <= n-1). Cost = nums[j].\n    \n    We need to find indices i and j such that nums[0] + nums[i] + nums[j] is minimized.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    min_sum = float('inf')\n    \n    # The first element is always nums[0]\n    # We iterate through all possible starting positions for the 2nd and 3rd subarrays\n    for i in range(1, n - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            current_sum = nums[0] + nums[i] + nums[j]\n            if current_sum < min_sum:\n                min_sum = current_sum\n                \n    return min_sum\n```",
