      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport bisect\n\ndef beautifulIndices(s: str, a: str, b: str, k: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the array of beautiful indices in sorted order.\n    An index i is beautiful if s[i...i+len(a)-1] == a and there exists\n    an index j such that s[j...j+len(b)-1] == b and |i - j| <= k.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Find all occurrences of string a in s\n    indices_a = []\n    start = 0\n    while True:\n        idx = s.find(a, start)\n        if idx == -1:\n            break\n        indices_a.append(idx)\n        start = idx + 1\n        \n    # Find all occurrences of string b in s\n    indices_b = []\n    start = 0\n    while True:\n        idx = s.find(b, start)\n        if idx == -1:\n            break\n        indices_b.append(idx)\n        start = idx + 1\n        \n    if not indices_a or not indices_b:\n        return []\n    \n    beautiful = []\n    # For each occurrence of a, check if there's an occurrence of b within distance k\n    for i in indices_a:\n        # Use binary search to find the closest index in indices_b\n        # Find the first index j in indices_b such that j >= i - k\n        pos = bisect.bisect_left(indices_b, i - k)\n        \n        # Check if the found index j satisfies j <= i + k\n        if pos < len(indices_b) and indices_b[pos] <= i + k:\n            beautiful.append(i)\n            \n    return beautiful\n```",
