      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef lastVisitedIntegers(words):\n    nums = []\n    result = []\n    k = 0\n    \n    for word in words:\n        if word == \"prev\":\n            k += 1\n            # If the number of consecutive 'prev' strings is greater than\n            # the number of integers encountered, return -1.\n            if k > len(nums):\n                result.append(-1)\n            else:\n                # The (k-1)-th index of the reversed nums array is\n                # the same as the element at index len(nums) - k.\n                result.append(nums[-k])\n        else:\n            # Reset consecutive count and add the integer to our history.\n            k = 0\n            nums.append(int(word))\n            \n    return result\n```",
