    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getGoodIndices(variables, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines which indices i in variables satisfy the condition:\n    ((a_i^b_i % 10)^c_i) % m_i == target\n    \"\"\"\n    good_indices = []\n    for i in range(len(variables)):\n        a, b, c, m = variables[i]\n        \n        # Step 1: Calculate (a^b % 10)\n        # pow(base, exp, mod) is efficient for large exponents\n        first_part = pow(a, b, 10)\n        \n        # Step 2: Calculate (first_part^c % m)\n        result = pow(first_part, c, m)\n        \n        if result == target:\n            good_indices.append(i)\n            \n    return good_indices\n```",
