    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum palindromic cube number not greater than N.\n    Since N can be up to 10^18, the cube root of N is up to 10^6.\n    We can iterate through all integers x from 1 up to 10^6, calculate x^3,\n    check if it's a palindrome and <= N, and track the maximum.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read N from standard input\n    line = sys.stdin.readline()\n    if not line:\n        return\n    n = int(line.strip())\n    \n    max_pal_cube = 0\n    \n    # The maximum possible value for x is the cube root of 10^18, which is 1,000,000.\n    # We iterate from 1 up to the cube root of N.\n    x = 1\n    while True:\n        cube = x * x * x\n        if cube > n:\n            break\n        \n        # Convert cube to string to check if it is a palindrome\n        s = str(cube)\n        if s == s[::-1]:\n            max_pal_cube = cube\n            \n        x += 1\n    \n    print(max_pal_cube)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
