    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input string and strip whitespace\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if not s:\n        return\n    \n    n = len(s)\n    # A parenthesis string must have an even length\n    if n % 2 != 0:\n        print(0)\n        return\n\n    MOD = 998244353\n    \n    # dp[i] will store the number of ways to have a balance of 'i'\n    # balance is (number of '(') - (number of ')')\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1\n    \n    for char in s:\n        new_dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n        if char == '(':\n            # Balance increases by 1\n            for i in range(n):\n                new_dp[i+1] = dp[i]\n        elif char == ')':\n            # Balance decreases by 1, but cannot go below 0\n            for i in range(1, n + 1):\n                new_dp[i-1] = dp[i]\n        else: # char == '?'\n            # Can be '(' (balance +1) or ')' (balance -1)\n            for i in range(n):\n                new_dp[i+1] = (new_dp[i+1] + dp[i]) % MOD\n            for i in range(1, n + 1):\n                new_dp[i-1] = (new_dp[i-1] + dp[i]) % MOD\n        dp = new_dp\n\n    # The result is the number of ways to end with a balance of 0\n    print(dp[0])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
