    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countAlternatingSubarrays(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of alternating subarrays in a binary array.\n    \n    An alternating subarray is defined as one where no two adjacent elements \n    have the same value. For a sequence of length 'L' that is alternating, \n    the number of alternating subarrays within it is L * (L + 1) // 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n    \n    total_count = 0\n    current_length = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        # If the current element is different from the previous one, \n        # it continues the alternating sequence.\n        if nums[i] != nums[i-1]:\n            current_length += 1\n        else:\n            # When the sequence breaks, calculate the number of subarrays \n            # formed by the previous alternating sequence and reset length.\n            total_count += (current_length * (current_length + 1)) // 2\n            current_length = 1\n            \n    # Add the count for the final sequence\n    total_count += (current_length * (current_length + 1)) // 2\n    \n    return total_count\n```",
