    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_45",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a 0-indexed integer array nums containing n distinct positive integers. A permutation of nums is called special if:\n\nFor all indexes 0 <= i < n - 1, either nums[i] % nums[i+1] == 0 or nums[i+1] % nums[i] == 0.\n\nReturn the total number of special permutations. As the answer could be large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [2,3,6]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,6,2] and [2,6,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [1,4,3]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,1,4] and [4,1,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= nums.length <= 14\n1 <= nums[i] <= 10^9",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef specialPermutations(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Precompute divisibility to speed up transitions\n    # adj[i] contains indices j such that nums[i] % nums[j] == 0 or nums[j] % nums[i] == 0\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i != j:\n                if nums[i] % nums[j] == 0 or nums[j] % nums[i] == 0:\n                    adj[i].append(j)\n                    \n    # dp[mask][last_idx] stores the number of permutations using elements in 'mask'\n    # ending with the element at 'last_idx'\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(1 << n)]\n    \n    # Base case: single elements\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[1 << i][i] = 1\n        \n    # Fill DP table\n    for mask in range(1, 1 << n):\n        for last in range(n):\n            if not (mask & (1 << last)):\n                continue\n            if dp[mask][last] == 0:\n                continue\n            \n            # Try adding a new element to the permutation\n            for next_idx in adj[last]:\n                if not (mask & (1 << next_idx)):\n                    new_mask = mask | (1 << next_idx)\n                    dp[new_mask][next_idx] = (dp[new_mask][next_idx] + dp[mask][last]) % MOD\n                    \n    # Sum up all permutations that use all elements\n    full_mask = (1 << n) - 1\n    result = sum(dp[full_mask]) % MOD\n    return result\n```",
