    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCost(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    To make all characters equal, we only need to perform an operation \n    whenever we encounter a boundary between two different characters \n    (i.e., s[i] != s[i+1]).\n    \n    For each such boundary at index i, we have two choices to align the \n    characters:\n    1. Invert the prefix [0...i], cost = i + 1\n    2. Invert the suffix [i+1...n-1], cost = n - (i + 1)\n    \n    We take the minimum of these two costs for every transition to minimize \n    the total cost.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    total_cost = 0\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if s[i] != s[i + 1]:\n            # Cost to flip prefix vs cost to flip suffix\n            total_cost += min(i + 1, n - i - 1)\n    return total_cost\n```",
