      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    The problem asks for the total cost of breaking down N into 1s.\n    The operation is: replace x with floor(x/2) and ceil(x/2) at cost x.\n    \n    Let f(x) be the total cost for an integer x.\n    If x < 2, f(x) = 0.\n    If x >= 2, f(x) = x + f(floor(x/2)) + f(ceil(x/2)).\n    \n    Since N can be up to 10^17, we use memoization to avoid redundant calculations.\n    The number of distinct values of x encountered during the recursion is small (O(log N)).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read N from stdin\n    line = sys.stdin.readline()\n    if not line:\n        return\n    n = int(line.strip())\n    \n    memo = {}\n\n    def calculate_cost(x):\n        if x < 2:\n            return 0\n        if x in memo:\n            return memo[x]\n        \n        # The recurrence: cost of x is x plus the costs of its two halves\n        res = x + calculate_cost(x // 2) + calculate_cost((x + 1) // 2)\n        memo[x] = res\n        return res\n\n    print(calculate_cost(n))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
