    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumOperations(num: str) -> int:\n    n = len(num)\n    # A number is divisible by 25 if it ends in \"00\", \"25\", \"50\", or \"75\".\n    # Special case: a single \"0\" is also divisible by 25.\n    targets = [\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"]\n    min_ops = n  # Initial max operations (deleting everything results in '0')\n\n    # Check if '0' exists in the string. If it does, we can keep one '0' and delete everything else.\n    if '0' in num:\n        min_ops = n - 1\n\n    for target in targets:\n        # Look for the second digit of the target starting from the end\n        i = n - 1\n        while i >= 0 and num[i] != target[1]:\n            i -= 1\n        \n        if i >= 0:\n            # Look for the first digit of the target to the left of the second digit\n            j = i - 1\n            while j >= 0 and num[j] != target[0]:\n                j -= 1\n            \n            if j >= 0:\n                # Operations required:\n                # (n - 1 - i) digits to the right of target[1]\n                # (i - 1 - j) digits between target[0] and target[1]\n                ops = (n - 1 - i) + (i - 1 - j)\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, ops)\n\n    return min_ops\n```",
