      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    m = int(input_data[0])\n    s1 = input_data[1]\n    s2 = input_data[2]\n    s3 = input_data[3]\n    \n    min_total_time = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try each possible digit (0-9) that all reels could stop on\n    for digit in '0123456789':\n        # Find all positions (indices) where this digit appears in each reel\n        pos1 = [i for i, char in enumerate(s1) if char == digit]\n        pos2 = [i for i, char in enumerate(s2) if char == digit]\n        pos3 = [i for i, char in enumerate(s3) if char == digit]\n        \n        # If any reel doesn't contain the digit, it's impossible for this digit\n        if not pos1 or not pos2 or not pos3:\n            continue\n        \n        # Try every combination of indices where the digit appears\n        for p1 in pos1:\n            for p2 in pos2:\n                for p3 in pos3:\n                    # The reels stop at times t1, t2, t3 such that\n                    # t_i % M = p_i\n                    # t_i = k_i * M + p_i\n                    # We need to assign distinct t_i values (since only one button can be pressed per second)\n                    # and minimize max(t1, t2, t3).\n                    \n                    # The possible candidates for t_i are p_i, p_i + M, p_i + 2M...\n                    # Since we only have 3 reels, the optimal t_i will not exceed p_i + 2*M\n                    times = [p1, p2, p3]\n                    \n                    # We need to find non-negative integers k1, k2, k3 such that\n                    # t1 = k1*M + p1, t2 = k2*M + p2, t3 = k3*M + p3 are distinct\n                    # and max(t1, t2, t3) is minimized.\n                    # Since M is small and the number of reels is very small (3),\n                    # we can iterate through small values of k_i.\n                    \n                    for k1 in range(3):\n                        for k2 in range(3):\n                            for k3 in range(3):\n                                t1 = k1 * m + p1\n                                t2 = k2 * m + p2\n                                t3 = k3 * m + p3\n                                \n                                # Check if all stop times are distinct\n                                if t1 != t2 and t2 != t3 and t1 != t3:\n                                    current_max = max(t1, t2, t3)\n                                    if current_max < min_total_time:\n                                        min_total_time = current_max\n                                        \n    if min_total_time == float('inf'):\n        print(\"-1\")\n    else:\n        print(min_total_time)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
