      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumJumps(nums, target):\n    n = len(nums)\n    # dp[i] will store the maximum number of jumps to reach index i\n    # Initialize with -1 to indicate that the index is unreachable\n    dp = [-1] * n\n    \n    # Starting position\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through each index to calculate the max jumps to reach it\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(j):\n            # Check if index i is reachable and if the jump to j is within the target range\n            if dp[i] != -1 and abs(nums[j] - nums[i]) <= target:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[i] + 1)\n                \n    return dp[n - 1]\n```",
