    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestSubsequence(nums, target):\n    # Initialize a DP table where dp[i] is the maximum length of a subsequence \n    # that sums up to i. We use -1 to indicate that the sum i is unreachable.\n    dp = [-1] * (target + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0  # Base case: sum of 0 is achieved by an empty subsequence\n    \n    for num in nums:\n        # Iterate backwards through the DP table to ensure each number \n        # from the original array is used at most once for each sum.\n        for i in range(target, num - 1, -1):\n            if dp[i - num] != -1:\n                # Update the max length for sum 'i' if using 'num' results in a longer subsequence\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[i - num] + 1)\n                \n    return dp[target]\n```",
