      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxSum(nums1, nums2, queries):\n    n = len(nums1)\n    # Combine nums1, nums2 into pairs and sort them by nums1 descending\n    pairs = sorted(zip(nums1, nums2), key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    \n    # Store queries with their original indices to return the answer in order\n    # Sort queries by x_i descending\n    sorted_queries = sorted(enumerate(queries), key=lambda x: x[1][0], reverse=True)\n    \n    ans = [-1] * len(queries)\n    pair_idx = 0\n    \n    # Since we need to find max(nums1 + nums2) where nums2[j] >= y_i\n    # and we've already filtered for nums1[j] >= x_i via sorting,\n    # we can use a Segment Tree or similar structure.\n    # However, given the constraints and the nature of the problem (y_i is up to 10^9),\n    # we need to coordinate compress the values of nums2.\n    \n    # Coordinate Compression for nums2 and query y_i\n    all_y = sorted(list(set(nums2 + [q[1] for q in queries])))\n    y_map = {val: i for i, val in enumerate(all_y)}\n    m = len(all_y)\n    \n    # Segment Tree to store the maximum sum for a range of y values\n    tree = [-1] * (2 * m)\n    \n    def update(idx, val):\n        idx += m\n        if tree[idx] < val:\n            tree[idx] = val\n            while idx > 1:\n                tree[idx >> 1] = max(tree[idx], tree[idx ^ 1])\n                idx >>= 1\n                \n    def query_max(l, r):\n        res = -1\n        l += m\n        r += m\n        while l < r:\n            if l & 1:\n                res = max(res, tree[l])\n                l += 1\n            if r & 1:\n                r -= 1\n                res = max(res, tree[r])\n            l >>= 1\n            r >>= 1\n        return res\n\n    # Process queries\n    for q_idx, (x_i, y_i) in sorted_queries:\n        # Add all pairs that satisfy nums1[j] >= x_i to the segment tree\n        while pair_idx < n and pairs[pair_idx][0] >= x_i:\n            n1, n2 = pairs[pair_idx]\n            update(y_map[n2], n1 + n2)\n            pair_idx += 1\n        \n        # Find the max sum among those where nums2[j] >= y_i\n        ans[q_idx] = query_max(y_map[y_i], m)\n        \n    return ans\n```",
