      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if not s:\n        return\n\n    # Count the frequency of each character present in the string\n    char_counts = Counter(s)\n    \n    # Count how many characters have a specific frequency 'i'\n    # freq_of_freq[i] will store how many characters appear exactly i times\n    freq_of_freq = Counter(char_counts.values())\n    \n    # The constraints say S length is up to 100. \n    # We check every possible frequency i from 1 to 100.\n    is_good = True\n    for i in range(1, 101):\n        count = freq_of_freq[i]\n        # The condition: there must be exactly 0 or 2 different letters that appear i times.\n        if count != 0 and count != 2:\n            is_good = False\n            break\n            \n    if is_good:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
