    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumSubarraySum(nums, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    To find the maximum sum of a good subarray where |nums[i] - nums[j]| == k,\n    we can use prefix sums. For a subarray starting at index i and ending at index j,\n    the sum is prefix_sum[j] - prefix_sum[i-1].\n    To maximize this sum for a fixed j, we want to minimize prefix_sum[i-1] where\n    nums[i] = nums[j] + k or nums[i] = nums[j] - k.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    prefix_sum = 0\n    # Map to store the minimum prefix sum encountered so far for a given element value.\n    # min_prefix[val] = min(prefix_sum[i-1]) where nums[i] = val.\n    min_prefix = {}\n    max_good_sum = float('-inf')\n    found = False\n\n    for x in nums:\n        prefix_sum += x\n        \n        # We are looking for a starting element 'start_val' such that |start_val - x| == k\n        # This means start_val = x + k or start_val = x - k\n        for target in [x + k, x - k]:\n            if target in min_prefix:\n                found = True\n                # Current subarray sum = current_prefix_sum - prefix_sum_before_start_element\n                max_good_sum = max(max_good_sum, prefix_sum - min_prefix[target])\n        \n        # Update the min_prefix for the current element x.\n        # The prefix sum 'before' the current element is prefix_sum - x.\n        before_current = prefix_sum - x\n        if x not in min_prefix or before_current < min_prefix[x]:\n            min_prefix[x] = before_current\n            \n    return max_good_sum if found else 0\n```",
