    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**Statement 1** is true because the softmax function generalizes logistic regression to multiple classes by providing a probability distribution over $K$ categories. **Statement 2** is true because the temperature parameter $T$ in a softmax function ($\\frac{e^{z_i/T}}{\\sum e^{z_j/T}}$) controls the \"sharpness\" of the distribution; as $T$ increases, the distribution becomes more uniform and its entropy increases. Since both statements are mathematically and conceptually correct, the correct option is \"True, True\".\n\n\\boxed{J}",
