    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9088",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many trees are there on 5 unlabeled vertices?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 6\nC. 8\nD. 10\nE. 11\nF. 12\nG. 15\nH. 9\nI. 7\nJ. 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of unlabeled trees on 5 vertices, we identify all non-isomorphic connected graphs with 5 vertices and no cycles.\n\nThe possible structures are:\n1. The path graph $P_5$ (a line: 1-2-3-4-5).\n2. A star graph $S_5$ (one central node connected to 4 leaves).\n3. A \"T-shape\" or branched tree (a path $P_4$ with one node attached to an internal vertex).\n\nChecking the list of non-isomorphic trees for $n=5$:\n- Path: $\\bullet-\\bullet-\\bullet-\\bullet-\\bullet$\n- Star: $\\bullet$ connected to 4 others.\n- Forked: $\\bullet-\\bullet-\\bullet(-\\bullet)-\\bullet$ (one node of degree 3, one of degree 2, and three leaves).\n\nThere are exactly 3 such non-isomorphic trees.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
