  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9091",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Maximize the entropy $H(X)$ of a non-negative integer-valued random variable $X$, taking values from 0 to infinity, subject to the constraint $E(X)=1$. Use base 2 logarithm to evaluate $H(X)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 4.0\nB. 2.0\nC. 3.0\nD. 1.0\nE. 4.5\nF. 2.5\nG. 3.5\nH. 0.5\nI. 5.0\nJ. 1.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To maximize the entropy of a discrete random variable $X$ taking values in $\\{0, 1, 2, \\dots\\}$ subject to a fixed mean $E(X) = \\mu$, the optimal distribution is the **Geometric Distribution**.\n\nFor a geometric distribution starting at 0, the probability mass function is $P(X=k) = (1-p)^k p$. The mean is given by $E(X) = \\frac{1-p}{p}$. \nGiven $E(X) = 1$, we solve for $p$:\n$1 = \\frac{1-p}{p} \\implies p = 1-p \\implies 2p = 1 \\implies p = 0.5$.\n\nThe entropy of a geometric distribution is given by:\n$H(X) = \\frac{-(1-p)\\log_2(1-p) - p\\log_2 p}{p}$\nSubstituting $p = 0.5$:\n$H(X) = \\frac{-0.5\\log_2(0.5) - 0.5\\log_2(0.5)}{0.5} = \\frac{-1 \\cdot (-1)}{0.5} = \\frac{1}{0.5} = 2.0$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
