    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9108",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose we have the following objective function: $\\argmin_{{w}} \\frac{{1}}{{2}} \\norm{{Xw-y}}^2_2 + \\frac{{1}}{{2}}\\gamma \\norm{{w}}^2_2$ What is the gradient of $\\frac{{1}}{{2}} \\norm{{Xw-y}}^2_2 + \\frac{{1}}{{2}}\\lambda \\norm{{w}}^2_2$ with respect to $w$?\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda w$\nB. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda I$\nC. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + (\\lambda+1) w$\nD. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda$\nE. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w + X^\\top y + \\lambda w$\nF. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y - \\lambda w$\nG. $\\nabla_w f(w) = (X^\\top X + \\lambda I)w - X^\\top y + \\lambda w$\nH. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X + \\lambda I)w - X^\\top y$\nI. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda^2 w$\nJ. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w + X^\\top y - \\lambda w$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the gradient of the objective function $f(w) = \\frac{1}{2} \\|Xw - y\\|_2^2 + \\frac{1}{2}\\lambda \\|w\\|_2^2$, we apply standard rules of matrix calculus.\n\n1. The gradient of the first term $\\frac{1}{2} \\|Xw - y\\|_2^2 = \\frac{1}{2}(Xw - y)^\\top(Xw - y)$ is $\\nabla_w (\\frac{1}{2} \\|Xw - y\\|_2^2) = X^\\top(Xw - y) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y$.\n2. The gradient of the second term (the regularization term) $\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda \\|w\\|_2^2$ is $\\nabla_w (\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda w^\\top w) = \\lambda w$.\n3. Summing these two parts gives the total gradient: $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda w$.\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, it matches Option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
