    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9113",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the number of labelled forests on 10 vertices with 5 connected components, such that vertices 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 all belong to different connected components?\n\nOptions: \nA. 70000\nB. 50000\nC. 30000\nD. 55000\nE. 75000\nF. 60000\nG. 45000\nH. 100000\nI. 80000\nJ. 40000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we use a generalized version of Cayley's formula. The number of labeled forests on $n$ vertices with $k$ connected components such that vertices $v_1, v_2, \\dots, v_k$ belong to different connected components is given by the formula:\n$T(n, k) = k \\cdot n^{n-k-1}$\n\nIn this problem:\n- $n = 10$ (number of vertices)\n- $k = 5$ (number of connected components)\n- Vertices 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 are fixed to be in different components.\n\nPlugging these values into the formula:\n$T(10, 5) = 5 \\cdot 10^{10-5-1}$\n$T(10, 5) = 5 \\cdot 10^4$\n$T(10, 5) = 5 \\cdot 10000 = 50000$\n\nComparing this result to the options provided:\nA. 70000\nB. 50000\nC. 30000\nD. 55000\nE. 75000\nF. 60000\nG. 45000\nH. 100000\nI. 80000\nJ. 40000\n\nThe correct option is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
