    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For the signal f(t)=3sin(200πt)+ 6sin(400πt) + sin(500πt), determine the minimum sampling requency (in πHz) satisfying the Nyquist criterion.\n\nOptions: \nA. 550\nB. 1000\nC. 600\nD. 250\nE. 500\nF. 400\nG. 450\nH. 700\nI. 200\nJ. 800\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the minimum sampling frequency (Nyquist rate), we must first identify the highest frequency component present in the signal $f(t)$.\n\n1.  The signal is composed of three sine waves with angular frequencies $\\omega_1 = 200\\pi$, $\\omega_2 = 400\\pi$, and $\\omega_3 = 500\\pi$ rad/s.\n2.  The highest frequency is $f_{max} = \\frac{\\omega_{max}}{2\\pi} = \\frac{500\\pi}{2\\pi} = 250$ Hz.\n3.  According to the Nyquist criterion, the minimum sampling frequency $f_s$ must be at least twice the maximum frequency: $f_s = 2 \\times f_{max} = 2 \\times 250 = 500$ Hz.\n\nThe question asks for the frequency in \"$\\pi$Hz\" (which is a non-standard unit likely implying the numerical value relative to the Hz scale or simply Hz based on the options provided). Based on the options, the value is 500.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
