    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of frames destroyed, first calculate the transmission rate of Gigabit Ethernet, which is $1 \\text{ Gbps} = 10^9 \\text{ bits per second}$.\n\n1.  **Calculate the total number of bits destroyed during the noise period:**\n    $\\text{Bits destroyed} = \\text{Rate} \\times \\text{Duration} = 10^9 \\text{ bps} \\times 0.002 \\text{ s} = 2,000,000 \\text{ bits}$.\n2.  **Convert the average frame size from bytes to bits:**\n    $\\text{Frame size} = 1000 \\text{ bytes} \\times 8 \\text{ bits/byte} = 8,000 \\text{ bits}$.\n3.  **Calculate the number of frames destroyed:**\n    $\\text{Frames destroyed} = \\frac{2,000,000 \\text{ bits}}{8,000 \\text{ bits/frame}} = 250 \\text{ frames}$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
