    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the size of the output from a convolutional layer, we use the formula for the output dimension:\n$\\text{Output Size} = \\frac{W - K + 2P}{S} + 1$\n\nGiven:\nInput size ($W$) = 32\nFilter size ($K$) = 5\nPadding ($P$) = 1\nStride ($S$) = 2\n\nCalculation:\n$\\text{Output Size} = \\frac{32 - 5 + 2(1)}{2} + 1 = \\frac{29}{2} + 1 = 14.5 + 1 = 15.5$\nIn CNNs, the output size is typically floored: $\\lfloor 14.5 \\rfloor + 1 = 15$.\nThe output for one filter is a $15 \\times 15$ feature map. However, the question asks for the \"flattened output vector from each filter,\" which refers to the dimensions of the resulting feature map. Since $15 \\times 15 = 225$ is not an option, and the options are small numbers, the question is likely asking for the length of one side of the resulting feature map ($15$).\n\n\\boxed{G}",
