    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9147",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the number of labelled rooted forests on 6 vertices\n\nOptions: \nA. 12500\nB. 18000\nC. 14000\nD. 16807\nE. 10000\nF. 20000\nG. 15000\nH. 17500\nI. 13000\nJ. 12000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of labelled rooted forests on $n$ vertices, we use Cayley's formula extension. A rooted forest is a collection of rooted trees. According to a known result in combinatorics (often attributed to Cayley or related to the Matrix Tree Theorem), the number of labelled rooted forests on $n$ vertices is $(n+1)^{n-1}$.\n\nFor $n = 6$:\nNumber of rooted forests = $(6+1)^{6-1}$\n$= 7^5$\n$= 7 \\times 7 \\times 7 \\times 7 \\times 7$\n$= 49 \\times 49 \\times 7$\n$= 2401 \\times 7$\n$= 16807$\n\nComparing this result to the given options:\nA. 12500\nB. 18000\nC. 14000\nD. 16807\nE. 10000\nF. 20000\nG. 15000\nH. 17500\nI. 13000\nJ. 12000\n\nThe correct option is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
