  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9148",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A remote database contains 30 seconds of color motion-video. The video sequence is of the format (352 ́288 pixels) with RGB digitization at 30 frames per second. Find the the data rate for this motion-video in Mbits/s (3 sig. fig.).\n\nOptions: \nA. 69.6\nB. 64.3\nC. 45.6\nD. 91.2\nE. 60.8\nF. 78.4\nG. 56.2\nH. 82.5\nI. 73.1\nJ. 85.3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the data rate, we need to determine the total number of bits generated per second.\n\n1.  **Pixels per frame:** $352 \\times 288 = 101,376$ pixels.\n2.  **Bits per pixel:** Since the video uses RGB digitization, it typically uses 8 bits per color channel (Red, Green, Blue), totaling $8 \\times 3 = 24$ bits per pixel.\n3.  **Data rate calculation:**\n    $$\\text{Data Rate} = (\\text{pixels per frame}) \\times (\\text{bits per pixel}) \\times (\\text{frames per second})$$\n    $$\\text{Data Rate} = 101,376 \\times 24 \\times 30 = 72,990,720 \\text{ bits/s}$$\n4.  **Convert to Mbits/s:**\n    $$72,990,720 / 1,000,000 \\approx 73.0 \\text{ Mbits/s}$$\n\nComparing this result to the options, the closest value is 73.1.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
