    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To construct a directed tree (specifically an arborescence or rooted tree) from an undirected tree, one must select exactly one node to serve as the root. Once the root is chosen, the direction of every edge in the tree is uniquely determined (they must all point away from the root to ensure every other node is reachable).\n\nSince there are 100 nodes in the undirected tree, there are exactly 100 possible choices for the root, resulting in 100 distinct directed trees.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
