    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate the Hamming pairwise distances and determine the minimum Hamming distance among the following codewords: 00000,10101,01010\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 6\nC. 10\nD. 7\nE. 8\nF. 1\nG. 9\nH. 4\nI. 5\nJ. 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the minimum Hamming distance, we calculate the Hamming distance (number of positions at which the bits differ) between every pair of codewords:\n1.  $d(00000, 10101) = 3$ (bits differ at positions 1, 3, and 5)\n2.  $d(00000, 01010) = 2$ (bits differ at positions 2 and 4)\n3.  $d(10101, 01010) = 5$ (bits differ at all positions)\n\nThe minimum of these distances is $\\min(3, 2, 5) = 2$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
