    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9213",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider that the following two signals: $x(t)$ and $v(t)$ $$ x(t)=\\left\\{{\\begin{{array}}{{cc}} 1 & 0 \\leq t \\leq 3 \\\\ 0 & \\text {{ otherwise }} \\end{{array}} \\quad v(t)=\\left\\{{\\begin{{array}}{{cc}} 1 & 0 \\leq t \\leq 2 \\\\ 0 & \\text {{ otherwise }} \\end{{array}}\\right.\\right. $$ Let $y(\\tau)=\\int_{{-\\infty}}^{{\\infty}} x(\\tau-t) v(t) d t$. Let $\\tau=2.5$. Determine $y(\\tau)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 2.5\nC. 2\nD. 1.75\nE. 0.5\nF. 3.5\nG. 0\nH. 1\nI. 1.5\nJ. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $y(\\tau)$ for $\\tau = 2.5$, we evaluate the convolution integral:\n$y(2.5) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x(2.5-t) v(t) dt$.\n\n1.  **Analyze $v(t)$**: The signal $v(t) = 1$ for $0 \\leq t \\leq 2$ and $0$ otherwise. This limits the integration range to $[0, 2]$.\n2.  **Analyze $x(2.5-t)$**: The signal $x(2.5-t) = 1$ when $0 \\leq 2.5-t \\leq 3$.\n    *   $2.5-t \\geq 0 \\implies t \\leq 2.5$\n    *   $2.5-t \\leq 3 \\implies t \\geq -0.5$\n    So, $x(2.5-t) = 1$ for $-0.5 \\leq t \\leq 2.5$.\n3.  **Find the intersection**: The integral is the overlap of the intervals $[0, 2]$ (from $v(t)$) and $[-0.5, 2.5]$ (from $x(2.5-t)$). The intersection is $[0, 2]$.\n4.  **Calculate the integral**: $y(2.5) = \\int_{0}^{2} (1)(1) dt = [t]_{0}^{2} = 2$.\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, the correct value is 2.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
