    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the ratio, we calculate the time required to read a specific amount of data (e.g., 4,000 bytes) for both versions.\n\n**Version 1 (1,000-byte blocks):**\nTo read 4,000 bytes, the system performs 4 read operations.\nTime per read = Seek (25) + Latency (8) + Transfer (1) + OS overhead (1 + 10) = 45 msec.\nTotal time for 4,000 bytes = $4 \\times 45 = 180$ msec.\n\n**Version 2 (4,000-byte blocks):**\nTo read 4,000 bytes, the system performs 1 read operation.\nTime per read = Seek (25) + Latency (8) + Transfer ($4 \\times 1$) + OS overhead ($4 \\times 1 + 10$) = $25 + 8 + 4 + 14 = 51$ msec.\nTotal time for 4,000 bytes = 51 msec.\n\n**Ratio:**\nThe ratio of Version 2 to Version 1 is $51 : 180 \\approx 1 : 3.529$. Comparing this to the options, it is approximately 1:3.5.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
