  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9246",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that $(X, Y, Z)$ are jointly Gaussian and that $X \\rightarrow Y \\rightarrow Z$ forms a Markov chain. Let $X$ and $Y$ have correlation coefficient 0.1 and let $Y$ and $Z$ have correlation coefficient 0.9. Find $I(X;Z)$ in bits.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.45\nB. 1.2\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.9\nE. 0.00587\nF. 0.15\nG. 0.6\nH. 0.7\nI. 0.025\nJ. 0.3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the mutual information $I(X; Z)$, we first determine the correlation coefficient $\\rho_{XZ}$. For a Markov chain $X \\rightarrow Y \\rightarrow Z$ where the variables are jointly Gaussian, the correlation coefficients multiply:\n$$\\rho_{XZ} = \\rho_{XY} \\cdot \\rho_{YZ} = 0.1 \\cdot 0.9 = 0.09$$\nThe mutual information between two Gaussian variables is given by the formula:\n$$I(X; Z) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 - \\rho_{XZ}^2) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 - 0.09^2) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 - 0.0081) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(0.9919)$$\nUsing the approximation $\\log_2(1-x) \\approx -x/\\ln 2$ for small $x$:\n$$I(X; Z) \\approx -\\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{-0.0081}{0.693} \\right) \\approx \\frac{0.00405}{0.693} \\approx 0.00584$$\nComparing this result to the options provided, Option E is the closest match.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
