      "generated_answer": "To find the value of $c_0$, we use the formula for the Fourier series coefficient $c_k$ with $k=0$:\n\n$$c_0 = \\frac{1}{T} \\int_{-T/2}^{T/2} x(t) e^{0} dt = \\frac{1}{T} \\int_{-T/2}^{T/2} x(t) dt$$\n\nGiven $T = 10$ and the definition of $x(t)$ over one period:\n$$c_0 = \\frac{1}{10} \\left( \\int_{-5}^{0} 2 \\, dt + \\int_{0}^{5} -2 \\, dt \\right)$$\n$$c_0 = \\frac{1}{10} \\left( [2t]_{-5}^{0} + [-2t]_{0}^{5} \\right) = \\frac{1}{10} \\left( (0 - (-10)) + (-10 - 0) \\right) = \\frac{1}{10} (10 - 10) = 0$$\n\nThe coefficient $c_0$ represents the average value of the signal over one period, and since the positive and negative areas are equal, the average is zero.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
