    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To convert the logical expressions to Reverse Polish Notation (RPN), we move the operators to the position immediately following their operands.\n\n**Expression (a):** `(Z \\downarrow ((((X) \\odot Y) / (X \\odot (Z))) > ((Y) \\equiv X)))`\n1. Inner terms: `(X \\odot Y)` $\\to$ `XY \\odot`; `(X \\odot Z)` $\\to$ `XZ \\odot`.\n2. Division: `(XY \\odot / XZ \\odot)` $\\to$ `XY \\odot XZ \\odot /`.\n3. Equivalence: `(Y \\equiv X)` $\\to$ `YX \\equiv` (or `Y \\equiv X` depending on notation, but RPN usually lists operands then operators).\n4. Comparison: `(XY \\odot XZ \\odot / > YX \\equiv)` $\\to$ `XY \\odot XZ \\odot / YX \\equiv >`.\n5. Final operator: `Z \\downarrow ...` $\\to$ `Z XY \\odot XZ \\odot / YX \\equiv > \\downarrow`.\n\n**Expression (b):** `(X / Y) / ((X / X) / (Y / Y))`\n1. Terms: `(X / Y)` $\\to$ `XY /`; `(X / X)` $\\to$ `XX /`; `(Y / Y)` $\\to$ `YY /`.\n2. Inner division: `(XX / / YY /)` $\\to$ `XX / YY / /`.\n3. Final division: `(XY / / XX / YY / /)` $\\to$ `XY / XX / YY / / /`.\n\nComparing these results to the options, Option B matches both derived strings exactly.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
