    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the dimensions of the resulting activation map, we use the standard formula for the output size of a convolutional layer:\n$O = \\frac{W - K + 2P}{S} + 1$\n\nWhere:\n- $W$ (Input size) = 32\n- $K$ (Filter size) = 5\n- $P$ (Padding) = 1\n- $S$ (Stride) = 2\n\nPlugging in the values:\n$k = \\frac{32 - 5 + 2(1)}{2} + 1 = \\frac{29}{2} + 1 = 14.5 + 1 = 15.5$\n\nIn CNN implementations (like PyTorch or TensorFlow), the result is typically floored: $\\lfloor 14.5 \\rfloor + 1 = 15$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
