  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9354",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $X_0, X_1, X_2, \\ldots$ be drawn i.i.d. from $p(x)$, and $x\\in\\{{1,2,3,\\ldots,100\\}}. Let $N$ be the waiting time to the next occurrence of $X_0$. Compute $E(N)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 99.0\nB. 101.0\nC. 125.0\nD. 150.0\nE. 50.0\nF. 25.0\nG. 175.0\nH. 100.0\nI. 200.0\nJ. 75.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $E(N)$, we first condition on the value of $X_0$. Let $X_0 = i$. The probability that any subsequent $X_n$ equals $i$ is $p_i = p(i)$. The waiting time $N$ until the next occurrence of $i$ follows a geometric distribution with parameter $p_i$, so the conditional expectation is $E(N | X_0 = i) = \\frac{1}{p_i}$.\n\nUsing the law of total expectation:\n$E(N) = \\sum_{i=1}^{100} E(N | X_0 = i) P(X_0 = i) = \\sum_{i=1}^{100} \\frac{1}{p_i} \\cdot p_i = \\sum_{i=1}^{100} 1 = 100$.\n\nThis result is independent of the specific distribution $p(x)$, provided that $p(x) > 0$ for all $x$ in the support.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
