  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9355",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are only three active stations in a slotted Aloha network: A, B and C. Each station generates a frame in a time slot with the corresponding probabilities p_A=0.2, p_B=0.3 and p_C=0.4 respectively. What is the normalized throughput of the system?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.700\nB. 0.275\nC. 0.250\nD. 0.300\nE. 0.528\nF. 0.452\nG. 0.600\nH. 0.485\nI. 0.350\nJ. 0.500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In a slotted Aloha network, a successful transmission occurs if exactly one station transmits in a given slot. The probability of success (normalized throughput $S$) is the sum of the probabilities that only station A transmits, only B transmits, or only C transmits.\n\nThe formula for throughput is:\n$S = P(\\text{A transmits})P(\\text{B doesn't})P(\\text{C doesn't}) + P(\\text{B transmits})P(\\text{A doesn't})P(\\text{C doesn't}) + P(\\text{C transmits})P(\\text{A doesn't})P(\\text{B doesn't})$\n\nUsing the given probabilities $p_A = 0.2, p_B = 0.3, p_C = 0.4$:\n$S = (0.2 \\times 0.7 \\times 0.6) + (0.3 \\times 0.8 \\times 0.6) + (0.4 \\times 0.8 \\times 0.7)$\n$S = 0.084 + 0.144 + 0.224 = 0.452$\n\n\\boxed{F}",
