    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9372",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the joint probability of H, U, P, and W described by the given Bayesian Network H -> U <- P <- W? [note: as the product of the conditional probabilities]\n\nOptions: \nA. P(H, U, P, W) = P(W) * P(P | H, U, W) * P(U | H, P) * P(H)\nB. P(H, U, P, W) = P(H) * P(U) * P(P | H) * P(W | U, P)\nC. None of the above\nD. P(H, U, P, W) = P(H | U, P, W) * P(U | P, W) * P(P | W) * P(W)\nE. P(H, U, P, W) = P(H) * P(W) * P(P | W) * P(W | H, P)\nF. P(H, U, P, W) = P(H) * P(W) * P(P | W) * P(U | H, P)\nG. P(H, U, P, W) = P(H) * P(W) * P(U | W) * P(P | H, U)\nH. P(H, U, P, W) = P(U) * P(W) * P(P) * P(H)\nI. P(H, U, P, W) = P(H) * P(U | H) * P(P | U) * P(W | P)\nJ. P(H, U, P, W) = P(H) * P(W) * P(P) * P(U)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the joint probability distribution for a Bayesian Network, you multiply the probability of each node given its parents.\n\n1.  **Analyze the Network Structure**: The network is defined as $H \\rightarrow U \\leftarrow P \\leftarrow W$.\n2.  **Identify Parents**:\n    *   Node $H$ has no parents: $P(H)$\n    *   Node $W$ has no parents: $P(W)$\n    *   Node $P$ has one parent ($W$): $P(P | W)$\n    *   Node $U$ has two parents ($H$ and $P$): $P(U | H, P)$\n3.  **Combine**: The joint probability is $P(H, U, P, W) = P(H) \\times P(W) \\times P(P | W) \\times P(U | H, P)$.\n\nComparing this to the options, Option F matches exactly.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
