    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9383",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider $x(t)$ to be given as, $$ x(t)=10 \\cos (20 \\pi-\\pi / 4)-5 \\cos (50 \\pi t) $$ What is minimum sampling rate (/Hz) such that $y(t)=x(t)$ ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 30\nB. 20\nC. 40\nD. 50\nE. 35\nF. 70\nG. 25\nH. 60\nI. 100\nJ. 80\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the minimum sampling rate (the Nyquist rate) for a signal $x(t)$, we must identify the highest frequency component present in the signal.\n\n1.  The signal is $x(t) = 10 \\cos(20\\pi t - \\pi/4) - 5 \\cos(50\\pi t)$. (Note: The term $20\\pi - \\pi/4$ in the prompt is likely a typo for $20\\pi t - \\pi/4$ given the context of sampling rates).\n2.  The first component has an angular frequency $\\omega_1 = 20\\pi$ rad/s, which corresponds to a frequency $f_1 = \\frac{20\\pi}{2\\pi} = 10$ Hz.\n3.  The second component has an angular frequency $\\omega_2 = 50\\pi$ rad/s, which corresponds to a frequency $f_2 = \\frac{50\\pi}{2\\pi} = 25$ Hz.\n4.  The maximum frequency is $f_{max} = 25$ Hz. The Nyquist sampling rate is $f_s = 2 \\times f_{max} = 2 \\times 25 = 50$ Hz.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
