    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What's the maximum number of edges in a simple triangle free planar graph with 30 vertices?\n\nOptions: \nA. 69\nB. 60\nC. 63\nD. 84\nE. 45\nF. 90\nG. 50\nH. 56\nI. 75\nJ. 48\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the maximum number of edges in a triangle-free planar graph, we use the property that for a connected planar graph with $v \\ge 3$ vertices, the number of edges $e$ satisfies $e \\le \\frac{3}{1} (v-2)$. However, if the graph is triangle-free (girth $g \\ge 4$), the formula becomes $e \\le \\frac{g}{g-2}(v-2)$.\n\nFor a triangle-free graph, $g \\ge 4$, so:\n$e \\le \\frac{4}{4-2}(v-2) = 2(v-2)$.\n\nPlugging in $v = 30$:\n$e \\le 2(30 - 2) = 2(28) = 56$.\n\nComparing this result to the given options, 56 corresponds to option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
