    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the storage requirement, we first determine the number of bytes per pixel for 4:2:2 YUV sampling. In 4:2:2, for every 2 pixels, there are 2 Y samples, 1 U sample, and 1 V sample, totaling 4 samples for 2 pixels, or an average of 2 bytes per pixel (since each component is 8 bits).\n\nThe total storage is calculated as:\n$\\text{Total Bytes} = \\text{Resolution} \\times \\text{Bytes per pixel} \\times \\text{Frame rate} \\times \\text{Time}$\n$\\text{Total Bytes} = (1920 \\times 1080) \\times 2 \\times 30 \\times (60 \\times 60)$\n$\\text{Total Bytes} = 2,073,600 \\times 2 \\times 30 \\times 3600 = 447,897,600,000 \\text{ bytes}$\n\nTo convert to Gbytes (using the standard decimal GB = $10^9$ bytes), we get approximately $447.9$ GB. Rounding to three significant figures gives 448 GB, which is closest to 450 GB among the options.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
