    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In Python 3, the `>>` operator is a bitwise right shift, which shifts the bits of the number to the right by the specified number of places. Shifting the binary representation of 8 (`1000`) one place to the right results in `0100`, which is 4 in decimal. Mathematically, `x >> n` is equivalent to floor division by $2^n$, so $8 // 2^1 = 4$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
