      "generated_answer": "To find the values of $B$ and $E$, we compare the given signal $x_1(t)$ to the complex exponential form.\n\nThe signal is $x_1(t) = \\cos(3\\pi t) - 4\\cos(5\\pi t - 0.5\\pi)$.\nUsing the identity $\\cos(\\theta) = \\operatorname{Real}(e^{j\\theta})$, we can rewrite the signal as:\n$x_1(t) = \\operatorname{Real}(e^{j 3\\pi t}) + \\operatorname{Real}(-4e^{j(5\\pi t - 0.5\\pi)})$.\n\nMatching this to the expression $x_1(t) = \\operatorname{Real}(Ae^{j\\pi Bt}) + \\operatorname{Real}(De^{j\\pi Et})$:\n1. For the first term: $\\pi Bt = 3\\pi t \\implies B = 3$.\n2. For the second term: $\\pi Et = 5\\pi t \\implies E = 5$.\n\nThus, $B = 3$ and $E = 5$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
