      "generated_answer": "To calculate the Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR) in decibels ($\\text{SNR}_{\\text{dB}}$) when given the voltage ratio, we use the formula:\n$$\\text{SNR}_{\\text{dB}} = 20 \\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{V_{\\text{signal}}}{V_{\\text{noise}}}\\right)$$\n\nGiven that the peak voltage of the signal is 20 times the peak voltage of the noise:\n$$\\text{SNR}_{\\text{dB}} = 20 \\log_{10}(20)$$\n$$\\text{SNR}_{\\text{dB}} = 20 \\times 1.3010 \\approx 26.02 \\text{ dB}$$\n\nRounding to three significant figures, we get 26.0.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
