      "generated_answer": "To prevent deadlock, one must eliminate at least one of the four necessary conditions: Mutual Exclusion, Hold and Wait, No Preemption, or Circular Wait. \n\n- **Option B and D** prevent Circular Wait by enforcing a strict linear ordering of resource requests.\n- **Option C** prevents Hold and Wait by ensuring a process obtains all resources atomically or none at all.\n- **Option A** only changes the order in which processes are served from a queue; it does not prevent a circular chain of dependencies from forming, meaning deadlock can still occur.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
