      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**.\n\nIn the Native Client (NaCl) design, the validator must forbid all instructions that modify segment state (such as `mov` to segment registers or `far` calls/jumps) to ensure the hardware-enforced sandbox boundaries remain intact. While indirect jumps (Option D) are restricted to specific patterns to ensure they land on 32-byte boundaries, they are not \"always forbidden\" in their entirety, whereas segment modification is strictly prohibited. Options B and C are incorrect because NaCl allows arbitrary memory access within the established segment limits.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
