    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine if an undirected graph has an Euler circuit, every vertex must have an **even degree**.\n\n1.  **Complete graph with 12 vertices ($K_{12}$):** Each vertex is connected to all others, so the degree of each vertex is $12 - 1 = 11$. Since 11 is odd, it cannot have an Euler circuit.\n2.  **Complete graph with 13 vertices ($K_{13}$):** Each vertex has a degree of $13 - 1 = 12$. Since 12 is even, it must have an Euler circuit.\n3.  **Tree with 13 vertices:** A tree with more than one vertex always has at least two leaves (vertices with degree 1). Since degree 1 is odd, a tree cannot have an Euler circuit.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is correct.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
