      "generated_answer": "To determine the number of bytes written to memory, we analyze the operations inside the loop.\n\n1.  **Loop Analysis**: The loop runs 256 times. In each iteration, the operation `A[i] = A[i] + B[2*i]` is performed. This involves reading `A[i]`, reading `B[2*i]`, and writing the result back to `A[i]`.\n2.  **Write Policy**: The cache uses a **write-through** policy. In a write-through cache, every write operation to the cache is immediately written to the main memory, regardless of whether it is a cache hit or miss.\n3.  **Calculation**: There is one write operation per iteration (`A[i] = ...`). Since there are 256 iterations and each element of array A is 4 bytes, the total bytes written to memory is $256 \\text{ iterations} \\times 4 \\text{ bytes/write} = 1024 \\text{ bytes}$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
