      "generated_answer": "To allow a single copy of a program to be shared by multiple users in a multiprogrammed system, the code must be **reentrant**. Reentrant code does not modify itself and keeps local data separate for each user (usually via registers or a stack), allowing multiple processes to execute the same code simultaneously without interference. While recursion often uses reentrant techniques, it is not a requirement for sharing, and being a macro is irrelevant to memory sharing.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{J}.",
