      "generated_answer": "To calculate $P(H|E, F)$, we can use Bayes' Theorem:\n$$P(H|E, F) = \\frac{P(E, F|H)P(H)}{P(E, F)}$$\n\nLooking at the options:\n- **Option I** provides $P(E, F)$, $P(H)$, and $P(E, F|H)$, which are exactly the terms needed for the numerator and denominator of the formula.\n- Other options (like B, E, or H) provide separate conditional probabilities $P(E|H)$ and $P(F|H)$; these are only sufficient if $E$ and $F$ are conditionally independent given $H$, but the prompt explicitly states we have no conditional independence information.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
