    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G**.\n\n**Explanation:**\nStatement I is true because virtual memory allows the execution of processes that are not completely in main memory, enabling a virtual address space larger than physical RAM. Statement II is false because only the currently needed pages must be in memory (demand paging), and Statement III is false because pages are fixed-size blocks of memory that do not correspond to semantic structures like functions or objects (which is a characteristic of segmentation).\n\n\\boxed{G}",
