  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9333",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following conditions can be expressed by a Boolean formula in the Boolean variables p_1, p_2, p_3, p_4 and the connectives ∧,∨ (without ¬)?\nI. At least three of p_1, p_2, p_3, p_4 are true.\nII. Exactly three of p_1, p_2, p_3, p_4 are true.\nIII. An even number of p_1, p_2, p_3, p_4 are true.\n\nOptions: \nA. None of the above\nB. All of the above\nC. I and III\nD. Only II and III\nE. III only\nF. Only I and II\nG. I only\nH. II and III\nI. II only\nJ. I and II\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine which conditions can be expressed using only $\\land$ and $\\lor$ (without $\\neg$), we must identify which conditions are **monotone**. A Boolean function is monotone if changing a variable from false to true can never change the output from true to false.\n\n1.  **Condition I (At least three are true):** This is monotone. If three variables are true and you change a fourth from false to true, it remains true. It can be expressed as: $(p_1 \\land p_2 \\land p_3) \\lor (p_1 \\land p_2 \\land p_4) \\lor (p_1 \\land p_3 \\land p_4) \\lor (p_2 \\land p_3 \\land p_4)$.\n2.  **Condition II (Exactly three are true):** This is not monotone. If exactly three are true (result: true) and you change the fourth to true, you now have four true (result: false).\n3.  **Condition III (Even number are true):** This is not monotone. If two are true (result: true) and you change a third to true, you now have three true (result: false).\n\nTherefore, only Condition I can be expressed using only $\\land$ and $\\lor$.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 253,
        "output_tokens": 282,
