  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9456",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the output of the following program READ (2, 3) I, J 3FORMAT (2I11) IF (I - J) 5,6,6 6WRITE (3,10) I 10FORMAT (1X, I11) GO TO 7 5WRITE (3,10) J 7STOP\n\nOptions: \nA. Prints the absolute value of the difference of two numbers\nB. Prints out the result of multiplying the two numbers\nC. Prints the second number twice\nD. Calculates the difference of two numbers\nE. Calculates the sum of two numbers\nF. Prints out the largest of two numbers\nG. Exits without printing anything\nH. Prints out the smallest of two numbers\nI. Prints out the result of dividing the first number by the second\nJ. Prints both numbers on the same line\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To analyze the provided program (written in an older version of FORTRAN):\n\n1.  **Input:** The `READ` statement takes two integers, `I` and `J`.\n2.  **Logic:** The `IF (I - J) 5, 6, 6` is an arithmetic IF statement. If `(I - J)` is negative (meaning $I < J$), it jumps to line 5. If it is positive or zero (meaning $I \\ge J$), it jumps to line 6.\n3.  **Execution:** \n    *   If the program jumps to line 5, it executes `WRITE (3,10) J` (prints the larger value).\n    *   If the program jumps to line 6, it executes `WRITE (3,10) I` (prints the larger value).\n4.  **Conclusion:** In both paths, the program identifies and prints the larger of the two input integers.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
