      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct answer, we evaluate each statement:\nI. **Throughput** is defined as $1/\\text{Clock Cycle}$. M-7 ($1/7.5\\text{ns}$) is greater than M-5 ($1/10\\text{ns}$), so M-7 has a higher maximum throughput.\nII. **Latency** is $\\text{Stages} \\times \\text{Clock Cycle}$. M-5 is $5 \\times 10 = 50\\text{ns}$, while M-7 is $7 \\times 7.5 = 52.5\\text{ns}$; thus, M-5 has shorter latency.\nIII. **Execution time** depends on pipeline stalls (CPI); because deeper pipelines often suffer more stalls, M-7 will not *always* be faster than M-5.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
