      "generated_answer": "**Statement 1** is **False**. For a continuous random variable, $p(x)$ refers to the probability density function (PDF). While the PDF must be non-negative ($p(x) \\ge 0$), it can take values greater than 1, as long as the total area under the curve integrates to 1.\n\n**Statement 2** is **False**. Decision trees are learned by **maximizing** information gain (or minimizing impurity/entropy), not by minimizing information gain.\n\nTherefore, both statements are false.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
