    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct option, let's evaluate the two statements:\n\n1.  **Statement 1:** The VC-dimension of axis-aligned rectangles is 4. However, for **non-axis-aligned** rectangles (rotated rectangles), the VC-dimension is 7. Since 7 is greater than 5, a set of 5 points can be shattered by the set of all rectangles in a 2D plane. This statement is **True**.\n2.  **Statement 2:** A 1-Nearest Neighbour (1-NN) classifier can shatter any number of points $n$ because for any arbitrary labeling of $n$ distinct points, the 1-NN rule will perfectly classify those points (each point is its own nearest neighbor). Thus, the VC-dimension is **infinite**. This statement is **True**.\n\nBoth statements are true.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
