    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the statements:\n\n*   **Statement 1 is False.** PCA performs eigendecomposition on the covariance matrix (size $d \\times d$, where $d$ is the number of features), while Spectral Clustering typically performs eigendecomposition on the Graph Laplacian matrix (size $n \\times n$, where $n$ is the number of data points). Unless $n = d$, the matrices are of different sizes.\n*   **Statement 2 is False.** While classification and regression are both supervised learning tasks, classification is not a \"special case\" of regression. Logistic regression is a classification algorithm that uses a logistic (sigmoid) function to map linear regression outputs to probabilities; it is not a \"special case\" of linear regression itself.\n\nBoth statements are false.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
