      "generated_answer": "The analysis of the statements is as follows:\n\n**Statement 1** is **true**. While the Expectation-Maximization (EM) algorithm is the standard approach for Gaussian Mixture Models (GMMs), GMMs can also be framed as an optimization problem using a likelihood function (or variational lower bound), allowing for gradient-based optimization methods.\n\n**Statement 2** is **true**. For a Gaussian-based Bayes optimal classifier, the learning process involves estimating the mean and covariance for each class. Since calculating these statistics involves a single pass over the dataset to sum the values and their squares, the time complexity is $O(N \\cdot d^2)$ (where $N$ is the number of records and $d$ is the number of attributes), which is linear in terms of the number of records $N$ for a fixed $d$.\n\nSince both statements are true, the correct option is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
