    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **I. assimilation**.\n\nIn Piaget's theory of cognitive development, **assimilation** occurs when a child fits new information into an existing mental schema (in this case, labeling a rabbit as a \"cat\" because it fits her existing category for small, furry animals). **Accommodation** would only occur if she modified her schema to create a new category specifically for rabbits. Therefore, using an old label for a new object is a classic example of assimilation.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
