      "generated_answer": "Heteroscedasticity refers to a situation in a regression analysis where the variance of the residuals (or the range of scores on the criterion) is not constant across all levels of the predictor variable. This is visually represented in a scattergram when the \"spread\" of data points widens or narrows at different points along the x-axis. Therefore, it indicates that the variability of the criterion changes depending on the value of the predictor.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
