    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The findings of Stanley Milgram's obedience studies suggested that situational factors and the presence of a perceived legitimate authority figure were more influential than individual personality traits or psychopathology. His research demonstrated that a high percentage of participants were willing to administer what they believed were lethal shocks simply because they were instructed to do so. Therefore, the study implies that atrocities can be committed by ordinary people under specific social pressures.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
