    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_72",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nA person is considered to have lived with you for all of the present year if the person was born or died in the present year and your home was this person's home for the entire time this person was alive.\n\nOptions: \nA. [(B ∨ D) • H] ⊃ L\nB. [L ⊃ (B ∨ D)] • H\nC. L ⊃ [(B ∨ D) • H]\nD. (B ∨ D • H) ⊃ L\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct symbolization, we first identify the logical structure of the sentence. The sentence takes the form \"A person is considered to have lived with you... **if** [the person was born or died... **and** your home was this person's home...].\"\n\n1.  **Identify the components:**\n    *   $L$: The person lived with you for all of the present year.\n    *   $B$: The person was born in the present year.\n    *   $D$: The person died in the present year.\n    *   $H$: Your home was this person's home for the entire time they were alive.\n2.  **Identify the operators:** The \"if\" introduces the sufficient condition (the antecedent), making the structure: $(B \\text{ or } D) \\text{ and } H \\implies L$.\n3.  **Symbolize:** $[(B \\lor D) \\bullet H] \\supset L$.\n\nComparing this to the options, Option A matches this structure exactly.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
