    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_49",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best English interpretation of the given arguments in predicate logic.\nDh ⊃ ~Pt\n(∀x)Px ∨ (∀x)Mx\n~Mb\t/ ~Dh\n\nOptions: \nA. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is a physical state. Either everything is physical or everything is mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\nB. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is not a physical state. Either everything is physical or everything is mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\nC. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is not a physical state. If everything is physical then everything is mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\nD. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is not a physical state. Everything is either physical or mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct interpretation, we break down the predicate logic symbols:\n\n1.  **$\\text{Dh} \\supset \\sim\\text{Pt}$**: \"If $\\text{Dh}$ (my headache is a dualist state), then not $\\text{Pt}$ (your tickle is not a physical state).\"\n2.  **$(\\forall x)\\text{Px} \\vee (\\forall x)\\text{Mx}$**: \"Either everything is physical or everything is mental.\" (This is a disjunction of two universal quantifiers).\n3.  **$\\sim\\text{Mb}$**: \"$\\text{Mb}$ is not the case (my broken toe is not a mental state).\"\n4.  **$\\sim\\text{Dh}$**: \"So, my headache is not a dualist state.\"\n\nComparing this to the options:\n- **Option A** incorrectly interprets $\\sim\\text{Pt}$ as \"is a physical state.\"\n- **Option B** correctly interprets all four lines.\n- **Option C** incorrectly interprets the $\\vee$ (or) as a $\\supset$ (if...then).\n- **Option D** incorrectly interprets $(\\forall x)\\text{Px} \\vee (\\forall x)\\text{Mx}$ as $(\\forall x)(\\text{Px} \\vee \\text{Mx})$ (\"Everything is either physical or mental\").\n\n\\boxed{B}",
