      "generated_answer": "The thinker described is **Ernest Nagel**, who explored these themes in his influential work *The Structure of Science* (1961). He argued that if theoretical terms cannot be fully reduced to observational language, the \"descriptivist\" view (that theories describe reality) becomes indistinguishable from \"instrumentalism\" (that theories are merely tools for prediction). This analysis highlights the logical difficulties in maintaining a strict distinction between the two positions within logical empiricism.\n\n\\boxed{Ernest Nagel}",
