    "global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_91",
    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One essay argues that this thinker discovered the survival of \"obligation\" long after the abandonment of the framework of divine law that made it \"really intelligible.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The thinker referred to is **G. E. M. Anscombe** (Elizabeth Anscombe). The essay mentioned is her influential 1958 work **\"Modern Moral Philosophy,\"** in which she argues that modern ethical terms like \"moral obligation\" are vestiges of a \"law conception of ethics\" that no longer makes sense without a divine lawgiver. She suggests that these concepts should be abandoned until a proper psychology of action is developed.\n\n\\boxed{G. E. M. Anscombe}",
