      "generated_answer": "To find the ratio of the insurance recovery to the incremental cost related to the closed Bridgeton landfill, we identify the relevant values from the text:\n1.  **Insurance Recovery:** The text states, \"we collected an insurance recovery of $40.0 million.\"\n2.  **Incremental Costs:** The text states, \"we incurred $12.0 million of incremental costs attributable to the bridgeton insurance recovery.\"\n\nThe ratio is calculated by dividing the insurance recovery by the incremental cost:\n$\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{40.0\\text{ million}}{12.0\\text{ million}} = \\frac{40}{12} = \\frac{10}{3} \\approx 3.33$\n\n\\boxed{3.33}",
