    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To estimate the parameters $\\beta$ and $\\gamma$ in the Cobb-Douglas production function $Q = AK^\\beta L^\\gamma$, the equation is typically transformed into a linear form by taking the natural logarithm of both sides: $\\ln(Q) = \\ln(A) + \\beta \\ln(K) + \\gamma \\ln(L)$. In this transformed state, the equation represents a linear relationship between the dependent variable $\\ln(Q)$ and two independent variables $\\ln(K)$ and $\\ln(L)$. This setup requires the use of multiple linear regression to solve for the coefficients.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
