try $0.31 \\times 2 + 0.31 \\times 4 + 2.60 = 0.62 + 1.24 + 2.60 = 4.46$.\nIf the rate was 31c for the first half ounce and 31c for each additional?\n$0.31 + (5 \\times 0.31) + 2.60 = 1.86 + 2.60 = 4.46$.\nLooking at the options, $4.62$ is E. $4.62 - 2.60 = 2.02$. $2.02 - 1.24 = 0.78$. $0.78/2 = 0.39$.\n$4.42 - 2.60 = 1.82$. $1.82 - 1.24 = 0.58$. $0.58/2 = 0.29$.\n$4.36$ is not an option. Let's re-read. Maybe 3% is 3.5 oz?\nIf 3.5 oz: $(4 \\times 0.31) + (3 \\times 0.26) + 2.60 = 1.24 + 0.78 + 2.60 = 4.62$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
