    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_370",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let’s assume Mutual Fund A has an annualized return of 15% and a downside deviation of 8%. Mutual Fund B has an annualized return of 12% and a downside deviation of 5%. The risk-free rate is 2.5%. What is the Sortino ratio for Fund A?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.2\nB. 0.8\nC. 2.0\nD. 1.0\nE. 1.4\nF. 0.95\nG. 1.8\nH. 2.3\nI. 1.56\nJ. 2.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the Sortino ratio for Fund A, use the following formula:\n$\\text{Sortino Ratio} = \\frac{R_p - R_f}{\\sigma_d}$\nWhere $R_p$ is the annualized return (15%), $R_f$ is the risk-free rate (2.5%), and $\\sigma_d$ is the downside deviation (8%).\n\nCalculation:\n$\\text{Sortino Ratio} = \\frac{15\\% - 2.5\\%}{8\\%} = \\frac{12.5\\%}{8\\%} = 1.5625$\n\nComparing this result to the given options, it matches Option I.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
