  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_51",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume the following model (from the preceding problem). Y = C + I + G C = 100 + 0.6Y I = 0.2Y - 50i M_D = 0.25Y - 30i M_s = 65 G = 100 whose equilibrium level was found to be 500. Suppose that full employment level of income is 600, so that the desired change is 100. If the money supply is held constant, what change in govern-ment spending will be required to close the deflationary gap?\n\nOptions: \nA. 80\nB. 75\nC. 55\nD. 90\nE. 50\nF. 61.5\nG. 70\nH. 85\nI. 100\nJ. 65\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the required change in government spending ($\\Delta G$), we first determine the multiplier of the economy. The equilibrium condition for income is $Y = C + I + G$. Substituting the given functions:\n$Y = (100 + 0.6Y) + (0.2Y - 50i) + G \\implies Y = 0.8Y + 100 - 50i + G \\implies 0.2Y = 100 - 50i + G$.\n\nSince the money supply $M_s$ is held constant, we look at the relationship between $Y$ and $G$ while accounting for the endogenous effect of $i$. \nFrom the money market: $65 = 0.25Y - 30i \\implies 30i = 0.25Y - 65 \\implies i = \\frac{0.25Y - 65}{30}$.\nSubstituting $i$ into the IS equation: $0.2Y = 100 - 50(\\frac{0.25Y - 65}{30}) + G \\implies 0.2Y = 100 - \\frac{5}{3}(0.25Y - 65) + G$.\n$0.2Y = 100 - \\frac{1.25}{3}Y + \\frac{325}{3} + G \\implies (0.2 + \\frac{1.25}{3})Y = G + \\frac{625}{3}$.\n$\\frac{0.6 + 1.25}{3}Y = G + \\frac{625}{3} \\implies \\frac{1.85}{3}Y = G + \\frac{625}{3}$.\nThe multiplier for $G$ is $\\frac{\\Delta Y}{\\Delta G} = \\frac{3}{1.85} \\approx 1.6216$.\nTo increase $Y$ by 100: $\\Delta G = \\frac{100}{1.6216} \\approx 61.66$. \n\nChecking the options, 61.5 is the closest value.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 268,
        "output_tokens": 501,
        "total_tokens": 769
      },
