  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_463",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You are planning to carpet a room 14'6\" by 11'3\". The price is $11.95 per sq. yd. Assuming that available widths are 15' and 12'. which is more economical? What is the cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15' width is more economical, $199.99\nB. 12' width is more economical, $275.95\nC. 12' width is more economical, $250.00\nD. 12' width is more economical, $199.99\nE. 15' width is more economical, $300.00\nF. 15' width is more economical, $250.00\nG. 15' width is more economical, $275.95\nH. 12' width is more economical, $224.06\nI. 15' width is more economical, $224.06\nJ. 12' width is more economical, $300.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the most economical option, we calculate the amount of carpet needed for each available width (15' and 12'), keeping in mind that carpet is sold by the linear foot of the roll width and then converted to square yards.\n\n1.  **15' Width:** To cover a room 14'6\" x 11'3\", we can buy a piece 15' wide by 11'3\" (11.25') long.\n    *   Area = $15 \\text{ ft} \\times 11.25 \\text{ ft} = 168.75 \\text{ sq ft}$.\n    *   Square yards = $168.75 / 9 = 18.75 \\text{ sq yd}$.\n    *   Cost = $18.75 \\times \\$11.95 = \\$224.06$.\n\n2.  **12' Width:** To cover the room, we must orient the 12' width across the 11'3\" dimension, requiring a length of 14'6\" (14.5').\n    *   Area = $12 \\text{ ft} \\times 14.5 \\text{ ft} = 174 \\text{ sq ft}$.\n    *   Square yards = $174 / 9 = 19.33 \\text{ sq yd}$.\n    *   Cost = $19.33 \\times \\$11.95 \\approx \\$231.03$.\n\nComparing the two, the 15' width is more economical at $224.06.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
