    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_52",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The average salary of the Bedford Manufacturing Co. rose 60% during a 10-year period. This rise amounted to $42.50 a week. (a) Find the average weekly salary at the beginning of the 10-year period, and (b) at the end of the 10-year period.\n\nOptions: \nA. $75.83, $118.33\nB. $90.83, $133.33\nC. $80.83, $123.33\nD. $55.83, $98.33\nE. $50.83, $93.33\nF. $70.83, $113.33\nG. $45.83, $88.33\nH. $85.83, $128.33\nI. $60.83, $103.33\nJ. $65.83, $108.33\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the average weekly salary at the beginning of the period, we let $x$ represent the initial salary. Since the 60% increase equals $42.50, we set up the equation $0.60x = 42.50$.\n\n1. Solving for $x$: $x = 42.50 / 0.60 = 70.833...$, which rounds to **$70.83**.\n2. To find the salary at the end of the period, add the increase to the original salary: $70.83 + 42.50 = 113.33$.\n\nComparing these values to the options, they match Option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
