  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_17",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: George is seen to place an even-money $100,000 bet on the Bulls to win the NBA Finals. If George has a logarithmic utility-of-wealth function and if his current wealth is $1,000,000, what must he believe is the minimum probability that the Bulls will win?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.525\nB. 0.800\nC. 0.450\nD. 0.575\nE. 0.750\nF. 0.350\nG. 0.650\nH. 0.300\nI. 0.700\nJ. 0.400\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the minimum probability $p$ that George believes the Bulls will win, we use the expected utility formula for a logarithmic utility function $U(W) = \\ln(W)$.\n\n1.  **Define the outcomes:** \n    Current wealth $W = 1,000,000$. \n    Bet amount $B = 100,000$.\n    If the Bulls win, wealth becomes $W + B = 1,100,000$.\n    If the Bulls lose, wealth becomes $W - B = 900,000$.\n\n2.  **Set up the expected utility equation:**\n    George will place the bet if $E[U(W)] \\ge U(W_{current})$:\n    $p \\ln(1,100,000) + (1-p) \\ln(900,000) \\ge \\ln(1,000,000)$\n\n3.  **Solve for $p$:**\n    $p (\\ln(1,100,000) - \\ln(900,000)) \\ge \\ln(1,000,000) - \\ln(900,000)$\n    $p \\ln(1.1 / 0.9) \\ge \\ln(1.0 / 0.9)$\n    $p \\ln(1.222\\dots) \\ge \\ln(1.111\\dots)$\n    $p \\ge \\frac{\\ln(1.111\\dots)}{\\ln(1.222\\dots)} \\approx \\frac{0.10536}{0.20067} \\approx 0.5251$\n\nThe minimum probability is approximately 0.525.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
