  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_438",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investor has utility function $U(x) = x^{{1/4}}$ for salary. He has a new job offer which pays $80,000 with a bonus. The bonus will be $0, $10000, $20000, $30000, $40000, $50000, or $60000, each with equal probability. What is the certainty equivalent value of this job offer?\n\nOptions: \nA. 100000\nB. 108610\nC. 110000\nD. 105000\nE. 90000\nF. 130000\nG. 120000\nH. 85000\nI. 95000\nJ. 115000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the certainty equivalent (CE), we first calculate the expected utility $E[U(x)]$ of the job offer. The possible total payouts $x$ are $\\{80000, 90000, 100000, 110000, 120000, 130000, 140000\\}$, each with a probability of $1/7$.\n\nThe expected utility is:\n$E[U(x)] = \\frac{1}{7} (80000^{1/4} + 90000^{1/4} + 100000^{1/4} + 110000^{1/4} + 120000^{1/4} + 130000^{1/4} + 140000^{1/4})$\n$\\approx \\frac{1}{7} (16.8179 + 17.3286 + 17.7828 + 18.2121 + 18.6121 + 18.9882 + 19.3433)$\n$\\approx \\frac{127.085}{7} \\approx 18.155$\n\nThe certainty equivalent is the value $CE$ such that $U(CE) = E[U(x)]$:\n$CE^{1/4} \\approx 18.155 \\implies CE \\approx (18.155)^4 \\approx 108,610$\n\nComparing this result to the given options, it matches option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
