    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_140",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose there is a 50-50 chance that an individual with logarithmic utility from wealth and with a current wealth of $20,000 will suffer a loss of $10,000 from a car accident. Insurance is competitively provided at actuarially fair rates. Compute the utility if the individual buys full insurance.\n\nOptions: \nA. 8.954\nB. 9.616\nC. 9.000\nD. 9.300\nE. 9.850\nF. 10.000\nG. 8.500\nH. 8.000\nI. 9.700\nJ. 9.210\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the utility if the individual buys full insurance, we first determine the premium. Because insurance is provided at actuarially fair rates, the premium is equal to the expected loss:\n$\\text{Premium} = 0.5 \\times \\$10,000 + 0.5 \\times \\$0 = \\$5,000$.\n\nWith full insurance, the individual's wealth is certain and equal to the initial wealth minus the premium:\n$\\text{Wealth} = \\$20,000 - \\$5,000 = \\$15,000$.\n\nThe individual has logarithmic utility, so we calculate the natural logarithm of the wealth:\n$U(15,000) = \\ln(15,000) \\approx 9.6158$.\n\nComparing this to the given options, it matches Option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
