    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_516",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ABC Plumbing has the following current assets and liabilities: Cash, $7,300; Marketable Securities, $14,200, Accounts Receivable, $2,120; Notes Payable, $1,400; Accounts Payable, $1,850. Find the acid-test ratio for ABC, correct to the nearest hundredth.\n\nOptions: \nA. 8.27\nB. 7.77\nC. 7.17\nD. 6.27\nE. 6.77\nF. 5.27\nG. 7.27\nH. 8.77\nI. 4.27\nJ. 9.27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the acid-test (quick) ratio, use the formula: $\\text{Acid-Test Ratio} = \\frac{\\text{Cash} + \\text{Marketable Securities} + \\text{Accounts Receivable}}{\\text{Current Liabilities}}$.\n\n1.  **Calculate Total Quick Assets**: $7,300 (\\text{Cash}) + 14,200 (\\text{Marketable Securities}) + 2,120 (\\text{Accounts Receivable}) = 23,620$.\n2.  **Calculate Total Current Liabilities**: $1,400 (\\text{Notes Payable}) + 1,850 (\\text{Accounts Payable}) = 3,250$.\n3.  **Calculate the Ratio**: $23,620 / 3,250 \\approx 7.26769$.\n\nRounding to the nearest hundredth gives 7.27.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
