    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_232",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nelson's Cycle Shop had a January 1 inventory of $30,156. During the month, new merchandise purchases totaled $28,300, and sales totaled $72,600. If the margin on sales was 45%, estimate the final inventory.\n\nOptions: \nA. $28,300\nB. $45,600\nC. $32,670\nD. $22,150\nE. $20,000\nF. $41,200\nG. $18,526\nH. $39,930\nI. $34,850\nJ. $25,400\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the final inventory, first calculate the Cost of Goods Sold (COGS). Since the margin is 45%, the cost percentage is 55% (100% - 45%).\n$\\text{COGS} = \\$72,600 \\times 0.55 = \\$39,930$.\n\nNext, use the inventory formula: $\\text{Ending Inventory} = \\text{Beginning Inventory} + \\text{Purchases} - \\text{COGS}$.\n$\\text{Ending Inventory} = \\$30,156 + \\$28,300 - \\$39,930 = \\$18,526$.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
