  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_580",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Owens Company accepted a draft, 90-day sight, amounting to $560 drawn on them by Watts Bros. Watts Bros, had the draft discounted 34 days before the due date at 6%. What were the proceeds?\n\nOptions: \nA. $560\nB. $550.00\nC. $555.00\nD. $558.50\nE. $562.00\nF. $558.00\nG. $563.17\nH. $556.83\nI. $553.83\nJ. $551.67\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the proceeds of the discounted draft, we calculate the discount amount based on the face value, the discount rate, and the time remaining until the due date.\n\n1.  **Identify variables:** Face Value = $560, Discount Rate = 6% (0.06), Time = 34 days.\n2.  **Calculate Discount:** $\\text{Discount} = \\text{Face Value} \\times \\text{Rate} \\times \\left(\\frac{\\text{Time}}{360}\\right)$ (using the standard banker's year).\n    $\\text{Discount} = 560 \\times 0.06 \\times \\left(\\frac{34}{360}\\right) = 33.6 \\times 0.09444 \\approx \\$3.17$.\n3.  **Calculate Proceeds:** $\\text{Proceeds} = \\text{Face Value} - \\text{Discount} = 560 - 3.17 = \\$556.83$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
      "success": true,
