  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_312",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TheMotorollaElectronics Company is taking inventory. It discovers that it has 30 widgets on hand. Records reveal the following information: Quantity Cost Per Unit Inventory, Dec. 2 6 $2.30 Purchase, Jan. 15 352 $2.50 Purchase, Feb. 4 101 $2.20 Purchase, Feb. 14 645 $2.00 Find the value of widgets in their inventory using the FIFO method of inventory.\n\nOptions: \nA. $120\nB. $45\nC. $55\nD. $30\nE. $85\nF. $60.00\nG. $110\nH. $75\nI. $90\nJ. $100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the value of the inventory using the **FIFO (First-In, First-Out)** method, we assume that the oldest items are sold first, meaning the remaining inventory consists of the **most recent** purchases.\n\n1.  **Determine the remaining quantity:** The company has 30 widgets on hand.\n2.  **Identify the most recent purchase:** The last purchase was on Feb. 14, consisting of 645 widgets at a cost of $2.00 per unit.\n3.  **Calculate the value:** Since 30 is less than 645, all 30 widgets are valued at the most recent price: $30 \\times \\$2.00 = \\$60.00$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
