    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_296",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that there are two firms in the market facing no costs of production and a demand curve given by Q = 150 - P for their identical products. Suppose the two firms choose prices simultaneously as in the Bertrand model. Compute the prices in the nash equilibrium.\n\nOptions: \nA. 30\nB. 50\nC. 0\nD. 25\nE. 150\nF. 75\nG. 90\nH. 120\nI. 100\nJ. 60\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the Bertrand model of price competition with identical products, firms compete by undercutting each other's prices to capture the entire market. This process continues until the price equals the marginal cost of production. Since the problem states that the firms face no costs of production, the marginal cost is 0. Therefore, the Nash equilibrium occurs where $P_1 = P_2 = MC = 0$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
