      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **I. Merton**.\n\nRobert K. Merton was a prominent sociologist who analyzed how the structural characteristics of bureaucracies—such as the demand for strict adherence to rules—can lead to \"dysfunctions\" in worker behavior, including the \"bureaucratic personality\" and ritualism. While Weber defined the ideal type of bureaucracy, Merton focused specifically on the unintended consequences and the psychological reactions of individuals within those systems.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
