  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_784",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assuming that each lived for the term of the policy, compare the cost of a $5,000 20-payment life insurance policy for a young man 25 years of age with a man 45 years of age.\n\nOptions: \nA. $3649 and $2207\nB. $2207 and $5000\nC. $110.35 and $182.45\nD. $5000 and $5000\nE. $1500 and $2500\nF. $182.45 and $110.35\nG. $4250 and $6250\nH. $2207 and $3649\nI. $3649 and $3649\nJ. $2500 and $4500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct answer, we must apply the basic principles of life insurance underwriting: the cost of a policy (the premium) increases as the age of the insured person increases due to the higher statistical risk of mortality.\n\n1.  **Comparison**: A 45-year-old man is older and thus represents a higher risk than a 25-year-old man, meaning the 45-year-old's policy will be more expensive.\n2.  **Evaluating Options**: We look for a pair of numbers where the second value (for the 45-year-old) is higher than the first value (for the 25-year-old).\n3.  **Selection**: Option H ($2207 and $3649) follows this logic, showing a lower cost for the younger man and a higher cost for the older man.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 273,
