      "generated_answer": "A white noise process is defined as a sequence of uncorrelated random variables with a mean of zero, a constant variance ($\\sigma^2$), and no linear dependence between values at different time steps. Consequently, the autocovariance is zero for all lags $k \\neq 0$, and equals the variance $\\sigma^2$ only at lag $k = 0$. Therefore, statements (i), (ii), and (iv) are correct, while (iii) is incorrect because autocovariances are not constant across all lags.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
