    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Dickey-Fuller test statistic is used to test for a unit root; it does not follow a standard normal distribution because the variance of the test statistic is smaller than that of a normal distribution under the null hypothesis. Consequently, the critical values for the Dickey-Fuller test are more negative (have a larger absolute value) than the critical values of a standard normal distribution for the same level of significance. This makes the test more conservative than a standard t-test or z-test.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
