      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**. In economics, \"token money\" refers to currency where the face value is significantly higher than the intrinsic value of the material from which it is made. This distinguishes modern coinage from historical \"full-bodied\" coins, which were valued based on their precious metal content (like gold or silver).\n\n\\boxed{D}",
