      "generated_answer": "The Augmented Dickey-Fuller (ADF) test adds lagged difference terms to the regression model to account for higher-order serial correlation in the series. This process ensures that the error terms (residuals) are white noise and free from autocorrelation, which is a requirement for the validity of the test statistics. Without this augmentation, the presence of autocorrelation would bias the results of the unit root test.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
