    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the context of econometrics and linear algebra, $\\hat{u}$ typically represents a vector of residuals. For a sample size of $T$, $\\hat{u}$ is a $T \\times 1$ column vector, and its transpose $\\hat{u}^t$ is a $1 \\times T$ row vector. The product $\\hat{u}^t \\hat{u}$ results in a scalar (the sum of squared residuals), which has dimensions $1 \\times 1$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
