      "generated_answer": "The Durbin-Watson (DW) statistic is related to the first-order autocorrelation coefficient ($\\rho$) by the approximate formula $DW \\approx 2(1 - \\rho)$. If the DW statistic is close to 0, then $0 \\approx 2(1 - \\rho)$, which simplifies to $\\rho \\approx 1$. Therefore, a DW value near zero indicates strong positive autocorrelation.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
