  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6301",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ray and Dorothy can both cook and can both pull weeds in the garden on a Saturday afternoon. For every hour of cooking, Ray can pull 50 weeds and Dorothy can pull 100 weeds. Based on this information,\n\nOptions: \nA. Ray cooks, since he has absolute advantage in pulling weeds.\nB. Ray pulls weeds, since he has comparative advantage in pulling weeds.\nC. Ray cooks, since he has comparative advantage in cooking.\nD. Dorothy pulls weeds, since she has comparative advantage in pulling weeds.\nE. Both Ray and Dorothy cook, since they both have absolute advantage in cooking.\nF. Both Ray and Dorothy pull weeds, since they both have absolute advantage in pulling weeds.\nG. Dorothy cooks, since she has absolute advantage in pulling weeds.\nH. Dorothy pulls weeds, since she has absolute advantage in cooking.\nI. Ray pulls weeds, since he has absolute advantage in cooking.\nJ. Dorothy cooks, since she has comparative advantage in cooking.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct answer, we must look at **comparative advantage**, which is based on opportunity cost. \n\n1.  **Opportunity Cost of Cooking:** For every hour spent cooking, Ray gives up 50 weeds, while Dorothy gives up 100 weeds. Since Ray gives up fewer weeds to cook, he has a lower opportunity cost and thus a **comparative advantage in cooking**.\n2.  **Opportunity Cost of Pulling Weeds:** Conversely, Dorothy gives up less \"cooking time\" per weed pulled compared to Ray, giving her a **comparative advantage in pulling weeds**.\n\nBased on the options provided, Ray should cook because he has the comparative advantage in that task.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
