      "generated_answer": "The most important disadvantage of the diagonal VECH model is that it does not automatically ensure that the resulting variance-covariance matrix is positive-definite, which is a requirement for the matrix to be valid. The BEKK formulation addresses this by using a quadratic form in its specification, which guarantees positive definiteness by construction. Therefore, the BEKK model overcomes this specific structural limitation of the VECH approach.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
