    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5741",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following assumptions are required to show the consistency, unbiasedness and efficiency of the OLS estimator?\n\ni) $E(u_t) = 0$\n\n\nii) $\\text{{Var}}(u_t) = \\sigma^2$\n\n\niii) $\\text{{Cov}}(u_t, u_{{t-j}}) = 0 \\forall j$\n\n\niv) $u_t \\sim N(0, \\sigma^2)$\n\nOptions: \nA. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (ii) and (iv) only\nD. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nE. (ii) and (iii) only\nF. (i) and (ii) only\nG. (iii) and (iv) only\nH. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nI. (i) and (iv) only\nJ. (i) and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the properties of the Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) estimator:\n1. **Unbiasedness** and **Consistency** primarily require that the error term has a mean of zero $E(u_t) = 0$ (i) and is uncorrelated with the regressors.\n2. **Efficiency** (according to the Gauss-Markov Theorem) requires the errors to be homoscedastic $\\text{Var}(u_t) = \\sigma^2$ (ii) and serially uncorrelated $\\text{Cov}(u_t, u_{t-j}) = 0$ (iii).\n3. **Normality** (iv) is required for conducting hypothesis tests (t-tests, F-tests) in small samples, but it is not required for the estimator to be the Best Linear Unbiased Estimator (BLUE).\n\nTherefore, assumptions (i), (ii), and (iii) are the necessary conditions for consistency, unbiasedness, and efficiency.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 297,
        "output_tokens": 210,
