  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6186",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following are plausible approaches to dealing with a model that exhibits heteroscedasticity?\n\ni) Take logarithms of each of the variables\n\nii) Use suitably modified standard errors\n\niii) Use a generalised least squares procedure\n\niv) Add lagged values of the variables to the regression equation.\n\nOptions: \nA. (iii) and (iv) only\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (i), (ii), and (iv) only\nD. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nE. (i) and (ii) only\nF. (i) and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (iii) only\nH. (ii) and (iv) only\nI. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To address heteroscedasticity (where the variance of the error term is not constant), several econometric strategies are commonly used:\n\n1.  **Logarithmic transformations (i):** Taking logs of variables often compresses the scale of the data and reduces the variance of the residuals, helping to stabilize the variance.\n2.  **Modified standard errors (ii):** Using Robust Standard Errors (e.g., White's standard errors) allows for valid hypothesis testing and confidence intervals even when heteroscedasticity is present.\n3.  **Generalised Least Squares (iii):** GLS (or Weighted Least Squares) specifically accounts for the structure of the variance to provide more efficient estimates than Ordinary Least Squares.\n4.  **Lagged values (iv):** Adding lagged values is typically a remedy for autocorrelation or omitted variable bias, not a standard treatment for heteroscedasticity.\n\nTherefore, (i), (ii), and (iii) are plausible approaches.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 263,
        "output_tokens": 207,
