    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5594",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements are true concerning information criteria?\n\n(i) Adjusted R-squared is an information criterion\n\n(ii) If the residual sum of squares falls when an additional term is added, the value of the information criterion will fall\n\n(iii) Akaike's information criterion always leads to model orders that are at least as large as those of Schwarz's information criterion\n\n(iv) Akaike's information criterion is consistent\n\nOptions: \nA. (ii) and (iv) only\nB. (ii) and (iii) only\nC. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nD. (i) and (iv) only\nE. (i) and (iii) only\nF. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (ii) only\nH. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nI. (iii) and (iv) only\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the statements:\n\n(i) **Adjusted R-squared** is often categorized as an information criterion in a broad sense because it penalizes the addition of unnecessary predictors to prevent overfitting.\n(ii) **False.** While the residual sum of squares (RSS) decreases when a term is added, information criteria (like AIC or BIC) include a penalty term for the number of parameters; if the decrease in RSS is small, the information criterion value will actually increase.\n(iii) **True.** AIC has a smaller penalty term ($2k$) compared to BIC/SIC ($\\ln(n)k$ for $n \\ge 8$), meaning AIC is more likely to select a larger model (overfit) than SIC.\n(iv) **False.** AIC is not consistent; as the sample size $n \\to \\infty$, AIC tends to overestimate the true model order, whereas SIC (Schwarz's criterion) is consistent.\n\nSince (i) and (iii) are true and (ii) and (iv) are false, the correct option is E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 289,
        "output_tokens": 229,
        "total_tokens": 518
      },
      "provider": "openai",
      "model_used": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
      "error": null,
