      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on the fundamental principle of international law known as *pacta tertiis nec nocent nec prosunt*, which is codified in the Vienna Convention on the Law of Treaties (Articles 34-36). This principle establishes that a treaty does not create either obligations or rights for a third State without its consent. Therefore, while a third State can be bound if it consents, it is not bound automatically.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
