      "generated_answer": "In *The Concept of Law*, H.L.A. Hart introduces the distinction between \"being obliged\" (a psychological state of being coerced) and \"having an obligation\" (a normative state created by a rule). He argues that this distinction is essential because it allows us to understand the nature of a rule as a standard for behavior, rather than merely a reaction to a threat. By isolating the normative element, Hart aims to illuminate the internal aspect of rules.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
