      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**. \n\nResponsibility to Protect (R2P) was developed to address the criticisms of \"humanitarian intervention\" by shifting the focus from a \"right to intervene\" to a \"responsibility to protect\" civilians, emphasizing prevention and multilateralism through the UN Security Council. Unlike traditional humanitarian intervention, which was often seen as arbitrary or unilateral, R2P establishes a clearer framework where the primary objective is to avert mass atrocities with international oversight.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
