    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1235",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calvin Poultry Co. offered to sell Chickenshop 20,000 pounds of chicken at 40 cents per pound under specified delivery terms. Chickenshop accepted the offer as follows: \"We accept your offer for 20,000 pounds of chicken at 40 cents per pound per city scale weight certificate.\" Which of the following is correct?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chickenshop's reply constitutes a counteroffer and no contract was formed.\nB. A contract was formed, but the terms need to be clarified.\nC. Chickenshop's reply constitutes a rejection of the offer, and no contract was formed.\nD. Chickenshop's reply constitutes acceptance of the offer, but the terms are subject to change.\nE. Chickenshop's reply constitutes a conditional acceptance, but not a counteroffer.\nF. A contract was formed, but it's not legally binding.\nG. A contract was formed on Chickenshop's terms.\nH. Chickenshop's reply is considered a breach of contract.\nI. A contract was formed but the terms are negotiable.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
