      "generated_answer": "The question involves the application of the Uniform Commercial Code (UCC), which governs the sale of goods. Under UCC § 2-207, a definite and seasonable expression of acceptance operates as an acceptance even if it states terms additional to or different from those offered, unless acceptance is expressly made conditional on assent to the additional or different terms. Here, adding \"per city scale weight certificate\" is a minor additional term that does not materially alter the contract, thus forming a binding contract.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
