      "generated_answer": "The proposal involves the creation of a new class of stock with priority over an existing class, which constitutes a material adverse change to the rights of the existing preferred stockholders. Under corporate law (such as the MBCA), when a proposal materially affects the rights of a specific class of shares, a separate class vote is required, regardless of whether the shares are generally \"nonvoting\" for other purposes. Since only 400 out of 1,000 preferred shares (40%) voted in favor, the proposal failed to receive a majority approval from the affected class.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
