      "generated_answer": "The question asks if the recognition of foreign judgments follows the same rules as the incorporation or transformation of treaties. The doctrines of monism, dualism, incorporation, and transformation refer specifically to how **international treaties** become domestic law. In contrast, the recognition and enforcement of **foreign judgments** (private international law) are typically based on the principle of **comity** or the **rule of reciprocity**, rather than treaty incorporation doctrines.\n\nAmong the options provided, Option E correctly identifies the discretionary nature of enforcement based on reciprocity, distinguishing it from the legislative processes of treaty incorporation.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
