      "generated_answer": "In the Hart-Fuller debate, H.L.A. Hart maintained a strict separation between law and morality (legal positivism). He argued that while the Nazi laws were morally abhorrent, they were legally valid because they were enacted according to the established rules of the system at the time. Therefore, he disagreed with Fuller's claim that the laws were \"invalid\" due to their lack of internal morality.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
