      "generated_answer": "The formal sources of international law, as outlined in Article 38(1) of the Statute of the International Court of Justice, include international conventions (treaties), international custom, and general principles of law. According to established international legal doctrine, there is no inherent hierarchy among these primary sources; they are applied based on the specific facts of a case, typically using the principle of *lex specialis* (specific law overrides general law).\n\n\\boxed{J}",
