    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The deed from the co-worker and boss to the neighbor created an **easement appurtenant** because it was granted for the benefit of lot 2 (ingress and egress) and specifically mentioned \"heirs and assigns.\" Easements appurtenant \"run with the land,\" meaning they are automatically transferred to the subsequent owner of the dominant tenement (the professor) unless specifically reserved. Although the deed was not recorded, it was valid between the original parties and transferred to the professor upon the sale of lot 2. Non-use (the neighbor's suspended license) does not constitute abandonment, which requires a clear intent to abandon.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
