      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on John Rawls's theory of justice, specifically the \"Difference Principle\" and the \"Maximin\" strategy, which suggests that parties in the Parties to the Original Position (POP) would prioritize the well-being of the least advantaged. While the POP is technically self-interested, they choose principles that protect those in the most vulnerable positions (such as the disabled) because they do not know their own status in society. Therefore, protecting the interests of the least well-off is the most consistent application of Rawlsian logic among the choices.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
