      "generated_answer": "The question concerns the scope of presidential authority under the separation of powers. While the President has broad authority over the executive branch, he cannot unilaterally direct federal employees to perform tasks that fall entirely outside the statutory authority granted to their agency by Congress. In this scenario, the agency's sole main function is border patrol to prevent illegal entry into the U.S.; directing them to conduct foreign emergency rescue operations lacks a basis in congressional authorization and exceeds the President's executive power.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
