      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G**.\n\nThe deed contains a \"right of re-entry\" (the power to \"re-enter and terminate the estate\") upon the breach of a covenant, which is the hallmark of a **fee simple subject to condition subsequent**. In contrast, a fee simple determinable would use language of duration (e.g., \"so long as\"), and an executory limitation would transfer the interest to a third party rather than returning it to the grantor.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
