      "generated_answer": "The tax structure is designed to ensure that both local studio owners and itinerant photographers are taxed for the privilege of conducting business within the city, without double-taxing those who maintain a studio. The credit provided to itinerant photographers who already pay the studio tax ensures that the tax is applied uniformly to the activity of commercial photography regardless of the business model. Therefore, the tax is a valid, nondiscriminatory exercise of the city's licensing and taxing power.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
