      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on the English legal principle that while extra-territorial abduction is an illegal act, it does not automatically divest the court of jurisdiction or necessarily constitute an abuse of process that requires a stay of proceedings. The general rule is that the court focuses on the legality of the charges and the interests of justice rather than the method of arrival, though it remains a matter of judicial discretion. In most reported cases, the abduction itself does not lead to a mandatory stay of proceedings.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
