    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1412",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The board of a state university has adopted the following rule concerning residency requirements:\"A student will be considered a legal resident of the state for the purpose of registering at the university if such person is over the age of 21 and has established a legal residence in the state for at least one year next preceding the last day of registration for credit. \"A student moved to the state and immediately enrolled at the state university. Since he did not fulfill the university residency requirement, the student was required to pay $1,800 tuition each semester, which was $400 more than the tuition of state resident-students. In an action by the student challenging the constitutionality of the provision governing the determination of residency for the purpose of fixing a fee differential for out-of-state students in public college, the court will most likely declare the provision\n\nOptions: \nA. unconstitutional, because it constitutes a violation of the equal protection clause of the Fourteenth Amendment.\nB. constitutional, because the fee differential promotes a compelling state interest.\nC. unconstitutional, because it constitutes a violation of the privileges and immunities clause of Article IV, Section 2.\nD. constitutional, because it is within the university's rights to set tuition fees.\nE. constitutional, because the provision does not trigger strict scrutiny.\nF. unconstitutional, because it constitutes a violation of the due process clause of the Fourteenth Amendment.\nG. unconstitutional, because it discriminates against out-of-state students.\nH. unconstitutional, because it infringes upon the student's right to education.\nI. constitutional, because it serves a legitimate state interest in encouraging state residency.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The issue is whether a state university can charge higher tuition to non-residents. Under the Equal Protection Clause and the Privileges and Immunities Clause of Article IV, states are generally permitted to charge out-of-state students higher tuition because the differential is based on the fact that residents have contributed to the state's tax base, which funds the university. This is considered a rational basis for the distinction and does not trigger strict scrutiny or violate constitutional protections.\n\nThe most accurate legal reasoning provided in the options is that the provision is constitutional because it does not trigger strict scrutiny (as residency is not a suspect classification and tuition is not a fundamental right), and it serves a rational basis. While several options suggest it is constitutional, Option E correctly addresses the standard of judicial review applied to such classifications.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
