    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**. \n\nUnder the federal Fair Housing Act (FHA), it is illegal to make, print, or publish any advertisement that indicates a preference or limitation based on race, color, religion, sex, handicap, familial status, or national origin. Even if the landlord's motive is to promote diversity, the act of publishing a racial or gender preference in an advertisement is a standalone violation of the FHA. While there is an exemption for owner-occupied buildings with four or fewer units regarding certain *rental practices*, this exemption does not apply to the publication of discriminatory advertisements.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
