    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In an oligopolistic market, the time series plot of **price** (specifically retail price, such as in gasoline markets) exhibits a sawtooth shape due to Edgeworth cycles. These cycles consist of a period of aggressive price undercutting followed by a sudden, sharp increase when firms return to a higher price level. This phenomenon is a classic example of dynamic equilibrium in markets with homogeneous goods and price competition.\n\n\\boxed{price}",
