    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a section of a paper titled \"The Problem Illustrated Anew,\" this man used an example from a law case in which a confectioner's mortars and pestles caused vibrations that prevented a doctor from using a stethoscope to examine patients; that paper by this man was published a few weeks before a Guido Calabresi article setting forth similar thoughts about liability rules in automobile accidents and is one of several of his papers that cite the case Sturges v. Bridgman.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
