    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question refers to the economist **Ronald Coase**, who famously analyzed the case of *Sturges v. Bridgman* in his seminal 1960 paper, \"**The Problem of Social Cost**.\" In this paper, he used the example of the doctor and the confectioner to illustrate the Coase Theorem and the role of transaction costs in legal liability. His work was published shortly before Guido Calabresi's influential article on similar themes in the *Yale Law Journal*.\n\n\\boxed{Ronald Coase}",
