  {
    "global index": "AIME_75",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Among the 900 residents of Aimeville, there are 195 who own a diamond ring, 367 who own a set of golf clubs, and 562 who own a garden spade. In addition, each of the 900 residents owns a bag of candy hearts. There are 437 residents who own exactly two of these things, and 234 residents who own exactly three of these things. Find the number of residents of Aimeville who own all four of these things.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of residents who own all four items, let $D, G, S,$ and $C$ represent the sets of residents owning a diamond ring, golf clubs, a garden spade, and candy hearts, respectively. We are given that every resident owns candy hearts ($|C| = 900$), so the total number of items owned is the sum of the individual sets: $195 + 367 + 562 + 900 = 2024$.\n\nLet $x_k$ be the number of residents who own exactly $k$ items. We are given $x_2 = 437$, $x_3 = 234$, and since every resident owns at least one item (candy hearts), $x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + x_4 = 900$. The total number of items owned can also be expressed as the sum $\\sum_{k=1}^4 k \\cdot x_k = 1x_1 + 2x_2 + 3x_3 + 4x_4 = 2024$.\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second gives $x_2 + 2x_3 + 3x_4 = 1124$. Substituting the known values $x_2 = 437$ and $x_3 = 234$ into this equation, we get $437 + 2(234) + 3x_4 = 1124$, which simplifies to $437 + 468 + 3x_4 = 1124$, then $905 + 3x_4 = 1124$, and finally $3x_4 = 219$.\n\nSolving for $x_4$, we find $x_4 = 73$.\n\n\\boxed{73}",
