    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find when the three cleaners will start cleaning at the same time again, we need to find the Least Common Multiple (LCM) of their cleaning intervals: 8, 12, and 14 minutes.\n\n1.  **Find the LCM of 8, 12, and 14:**\n    *   Prime factorization of 8: $2^3$\n    *   Prime factorization of 12: $2^2 \\times 3$\n    *   Prime factorization of 14: $2 \\times 7$\n    *   $\\text{LCM}(8, 12, 14) = 2^3 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 8 \\times 21 = 168$ minutes.\n\n2.  **Convert the duration to hours and minutes:**\n    *   $168 \\text{ minutes} = 2 \\text{ hours and } 48 \\text{ minutes}$.\n\n3.  **Add the duration to the start time:**\n    *   $14:15 + 2:48 = 17:03$.\n\nThey will start cleaning windows at the same time again at 17:03.\n\n\\boxed{17:03}",
