      "generated_answer": "Let the fraction be $\\frac{x}{y}$.\n\n1. According to the first condition, adding 1 to both the numerator and denominator gives $\\frac{x+1}{y+1} = \\frac{4}{5}$, which simplifies to $5x + 5 = 4y + 4$, or $5x - 4y = -1$.\n2. According to the second condition, subtracting 5 from both gives $\\frac{x-5}{y-5} = \\frac{1}{2}$, which simplifies to $2x - 10 = y - 5$, or $y = 2x - 5$.\n3. Substituting $y = 2x - 5$ into the first equation gives $5x - 4(2x - 5) = -1$, which simplifies to $5x - 8x + 20 = -1$, leading to $-3x = -21$, so $x = 7$ and $y = 2(7) - 5 = 9$.\n\nThe fraction is $\\frac{7}{9}$.\n\n\\boxed{7/9}",
