      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**.\n\nThe \"Three Worlds\" model was a Cold War-era classification where the First World represented democratic-industrialized nations, the Second World represented communist-socialist states, and the Third World represented non-aligned or developing nations. Because the \"Second World\" was defined by political ideology rather than a middle-tier level of development, the numerical ranking is often considered misleading in a modern economic context.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
