      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C**. \n\nAs a country transitions from an agricultural to an industrial base, traditional seasonal movements of livestock and people, known as **transhumance**, decrease as the economy shifts away from subsistence pastoralism. Industrialization promotes urbanization and sedentary lifestyles, making the nomadic or semi-nomadic patterns of transhumance less common. Other forms of migration, such as intraregional migration (rural-to-urban), typically increase during this transition.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
