      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **\\boxed{A}**.\n\nThomas Malthus argued that human population grows exponentially (geometrically), which is represented by a **J-curve** on a graph. He believed this rapid growth would eventually outpace the linear growth of food production, leading to catastrophic \"Malthusian checks\" like famine and disease. In contrast, the S-curve represents logistic growth where population stabilizes at a carrying capacity, a concept more aligned with modern demographic transitions than Malthus's original warnings.",
